' The player. The session reducer decides; this file feeds it the Video
' node's state, position, and errors (playback.video), ApiTask's answers
' (playback.player.answerEvent), and the viewer's seeks and track choices,
' and carries out its commands: requests through api.playback, content
' loads through one Video node (playback.slot), sidecar subtitles through
' ApiTask and MediaTask, and the overlay. Every Video callback is tagged
' with the load whose content the node has, so the reducer ignores what an
' earlier load reports.
'
' Keys go through the controls reducer (playback.controls, spec section 5.7's
' key table), driven by the controlsTimer for holds, the rate ladder, merged
' skips, and hiding. Its seeks are committed through the session reducer
' (seekTo: a local seek or a seek_reanchor), never by setting Video.seek
' here. While the controls hide, the Video node keeps focus, so * reaches
' Roku's caption and audio overlay; while they show, the overlay's empty
' keyFocus child has it and * opens Silo's Options (plan sections 6.4 and
' 6.10). Development builds log where focus is when the controls show or
' hide and when * arrives (logFocus). The profile's playback preferences
' (playback.preferences) are read beside the watch projection; the start
' waits for them up to PREFERENCES_WAIT_MS, because its audio, quality,
' and bitrate cap follow them, and the defaults apply when they fail or
' come later.
'
' Tracks (spec sections 8.5 and 9.7). A first start plays the version
' Detail's Versions menu pinned (nav.player.pinnedFile), else the start
' path's, and names Detail's picks for the version it plays
' (nav.player.tracksFor through
' playback.options.initialTracks); Detail's Auto, and a start without picks,
' name the version's effective audio track, else the audio the worker
' chooses for the profile's language and the device
' (playback.options.initialAudio), and no subtitle; the session's
' first plan then gets the subtitle the preferences choose from its
' inventory (playback.options.afterStart), with at most one track_change. Nothing at load changes Roku's caption mode (assumption
' AG-75): a subtitle the preferences choose shows while captions are on.
' A burned-in subtitle cannot follow the mode, so the plan follows it
' instead (followCaptions): captions Off asks for a plan without it and sets
' it aside, and any other mode asks for it again. The Video node draws only
' the plan's subtitle (Video.suppressCaptions, playback.sidecars.suppressed),
' never a track Roku picks itself, such as one in an original's container.
' A sidecar is selected by the TrackName Roku lists for it
' (Video.availableSubtitleTracks, playback.sidecars.listedName), and an
' in-place switch Roku does not follow reloads (checkSubtitle). Roku
' reports a selected sidecar by any name that contains its path
' (playback.sidecars.isTrack). The player selects nothing on its own while
' content starts (onVideoSubtitles): Roku stopped content it was opening
' when the player did (hardware run 20). Once the content settles, it
' selects the sidecar once if Roku plays another track (confirmSubtitle):
' Roku drew English while the sidecar of another language was selected
' (hardware run 21).
'
' Content on the Video node is never changed: Roku closed the player when
' playing content was given another subtitle track (hardware run 19), so a
' sidecar that comes late reloads (lateSubtitle). Content waiting for the
' node's stop may still change (its playStart and SubtitleTracks). The node
' itself takes only seeks, track selections (subtitleTrack, audioTrack),
' suppressCaptions, the caption mode, pause and resume, and its box;
' anything else is new content for a load the session reducer started, so
' nothing the replaced content reports reaches the stall clock. A
' "finished" right after one of those changes, before the content's end,
' is the change's doing, and the session reloads at the position
' (noteWrite).
'
' Options (playback.options, components/player/options/OptionsPanel): the
' Options button opens it on the tab it showed last in this player (Info
' the first time), and Down with the controls hidden on Video (spec
' section 5.7). * with the controls shown opens it on Video only on a Roku
' player that passes the key on: a Roku TV takes * during full-screen
' playback whatever has focus (assumption AG-117). It attaches under
' optionsLayer, takes focus on its tabs, and handles Back itself: the first
' Back closes its Quality picker, else the panel, and a pick leaves it
' open, whether the plan switches in place or reloads (hardware run 22).
' setOverlayFlags tells the controls reducer while it is open (options) and
' while focus is in its columns (picker), so the reducer leaves the keys to
' it; the controls step aside meanwhile, as tvOS's do, and come back when
' it closes. Quality and
' track choices go through the session reducer; a caption mode, and On
' when a subtitle track is chosen with captions off, are written to
' Video.globalCaptionMode, and a mode alone may need a plan that follows it
' (followCaptions); Auto-play next is Up Next's toggle too
' (m.autoplayNext). The model is set again whenever what it shows changes.
'
' Roku's * overlay: a track changed there is observed on the Video node and
' becomes a track_change or is written back (playback.options.watchOverlay);
' a caption mode set there arrives as a platform event, which the plan may
' follow (followCaptions).
'
' Seek previews (playback.trickplay, components/player/trickplay/
' TrickplayPreview): the manifest of the file the plan plays is read when the
' watch projection marks the file and capabilities list trickplay_v1, after
' the first plan, again when a replan changes the file, and when the preview
' asks (its URLs expire, or a sheet failed). The preview shows above the
' scrubber while the controls show a scrub, for Left and Right and every
' ladder speed, and the memory level sets the sheets it keeps.
'
' Platform events (source/platform/client.bs): the caption mode, the memory
' level, and a codec capability or HDMI change, which re-probes the output
' in ApiTask; the reducer replans only when the normalized output context
' changed.
'
' Markers (playback.markers, spec section 9.8): the version the plan plays
' gives the scrubber its bands and Skip Intro its intro ranges, read when
' the intent arrives and again when a replan changes the file.
'
' Skip intro (playback.skipIntro, components/player/skip/SkipIntroButton):
' positions and the Video state drive it, and the panelTimer its fill. The
' button places itself at the bottom right, raised while the controls show.
' While it shows (the controls reducer's skipButton flag), OK with the
' controls hidden, or on the pill when it has the controls' focus, arrives
' as activateSkip() and Back as dismissSkip(). Skip Recap
' (playback.skipRecap, SkipRecapButton) takes the same positions, Video
' state, and markers, shows while playback is inside a recap, and skips it
' itself under the profile's playback.auto_skip_recap; its OK arrives as
' activateRecap. Their seeks, Watch Intro's back to the intro's start too,
' go through the session reducer as every seek does (commitSeek: local or
' seek_reanchor).
'
' Up Next (playback.upNext, components/player/upnext/UpNextPanel), for
' every item, as tvOS's: after the first plan, an episode's next episode is
' resolved (playback.nextEpisode) and On Deck is read (playback.onDeck),
' both through ApiTask's catalog reads, and the controls' Up Next button
' shows while Up Next has something to show. The panel opens in the
' profile's prompt window before the end (playback.next_up_prompt_seconds),
' at the video's end, or from the button; it attaches under upNextLayer,
' takes focus, and shrinks the video into theme.upNext's box (setVideoBox).
' Back on it is Keep Watching. Auto-play next is one toggle for Options and
' the panel (m.autoplayNext): the profile's playback.auto_play_next, which
' the viewer's change writes for this device (writeAutoplay), and the
' countdown also needs roDeviceInfo.IsAutoplayEnabled().
'
' The next item starts in this player (assumption AG-100). Play Now, the
' countdown, or an On Deck card stops the session as Back does, with its
' final position and durable stop job (plan section 6.6); once the reducer
' is done, the player clears what was the item's (clearSession) and starts
' nav.player.nextEpisode's intent: where the item resumes, with the carry
' (the toggle), as an autoplay start unless the viewer chose an On Deck
' card. Keep Watching after the end starts the same item 10 s before its end
' the same way (nav.player.replay). The same Video node plays it once it has
' stopped (playback.slot), and load numbers keep counting, so a late
' callback of the item before never matches a load of the next. The stack
' entry stays the first item's: Back returns to the page it came from, and
' the pages beneath refresh once, when the player closes. Each next episode
' of the first item's series is noted on the entry (nav.notePlayed), so that
' page selects the episode the chain played last, and as the player leaves,
' so is its last item and whether this playback finished it
' (playback.upNext.leftFinished), which decides whether that page moves on
' (spec section 5.6). Once the chain moves to another title (On Deck), the
' notes stop at the last item of the first one (m.leftSeries).

const LOG_TAG = "player"
' The sidecar download's deadline. First extractions of embedded text take
' about 65 s on the reference file, so the plan's 10 s would always miss them
' (assumption A-15); "Loading subtitles…" shows meanwhile. New content waits
' for its selected sidecar up to a cap, and a little for the others
' (playback.sidecars.waitUntil); a selected one that arrives later reloads
' the plan to carry it (lateSubtitle).
const SUBTITLE_TIMEOUT_MS = 120000
const NOTICE_MS = 4000
' The keys the controls reducer takes; the others pass on.
const CONTROL_KEYS = "|back|OK|play|left|right|up|down|rewind|fastforward|replay|options|"
' Roku's caption mode that shows captions after a replay (plan section 6.10).
const INSTANT_REPLAY = "Instant replay"
' The failure screen (tvOS's PlayerView error): the 40 px triangle, 16 px
' over the title and message, which stand 16 px over the 62 px buttons, 16
' px apart, the stack centred on the screen.
const ERROR_WIDTH = 1200
const ERROR_GAP = 16
const ERROR_LINE_GAP = 8
const ERROR_ICON = 40
const ERROR_BUTTON_HEIGHT = 62
' How long the start waits for the profile's preferences once the watch
' projection has answered; both are read at once.
const PREFERENCES_WAIT_MS = 2000
' How long after an in-place subtitle switch, or the player's selection
' once content settles, Roku may still report the track before it as the
' one it plays (checkSubtitle, confirmSubtitle).
const SUBTITLE_CHECK_MS = 3000
' How long after its first frame content takes no subtitle selection the
' player makes on its own (holdsSubtitle).
const SUBTITLE_SETTLE_MS = 3000
' How soon after the player changes started content a "finished" is the
' change's doing (hardware run 20: 0.17 s after a subtitle selection).
const WRITE_STOP_MS = 2000
' How many such stops with one subtitle selected end the player's own
' selections of it until the viewer chooses a track (confirmSubtitle).
const WRITE_STOPS_QUIET = 2
' How long after Silo writes a caption mode Roku's first event may still
' repeat the mode before it (hardware runs 7 and 17).
const STALE_CAPTION_MS = 3000
' The hold indicator's chip stands this far under the preview's tile.
const HOLD_GAP = 16

sub init()
    m.video = m.top.findNode("video")
    ' The node's own agent, set before any content, keeps HttpHeaders off the
    ' global agent that Posters share (plan section 6.4).
    agent = CreateObject("roHttpAgent")
    agent.SetCertificatesFile("common:/certs/ca-bundle.crt")
    m.video.setHttpAgent(agent)
    m.video.asyncStopSemantics = true
    m.video.observeField("state", "onVideoState")
    m.video.observeField("position", "onVideoPosition")
    m.video.observeField("audioFormat", "onVideoAudio")
    m.video.observeField("videoFormat", "onVideoFormat")
    m.video.observeField("downloadedSegment", "onVideoSegment")
    m.video.observeField("bufferingStatus", "onVideoBuffer")
    m.video.observeField("audioTrack", "onVideoTracks")
    m.video.observeField("subtitleTrack", "onVideoTracks")
    m.video.observeField("availableSubtitleTracks", "onVideoSubtitles")

    m.overlay = m.top.findNode("overlay")
    m.overlayFocus = m.overlay.findNode("keyFocus")
    m.skipButton = m.top.findNode("skipButton")
    m.recapButton = m.top.findNode("recapButton")
    m.optionsLayer = m.top.findNode("optionsLayer")
    m.upNextLayer = m.top.findNode("upNextLayer")
    m.preview = m.top.findNode("preview")
    m.preview.span = [theme.player.LEFT, theme.player.RIGHT]
    m.holdIndicator = m.top.findNode("holdIndicator")
    m.status = m.top.findNode("status")
    m.preview.observeField("refresh", "onPreviewRefresh")
    m.errorPanel = m.top.findNode("errorPanel")
    m.errorIcon = m.top.findNode("errorIcon")
    m.errorIcon.setFields({ uri: "pkg:/images/player/warning.png", blendColor: theme.color.ERROR_ICON })
    m.errorTitle = styled("errorTitle", theme.textStyle.NOTICE_TITLE, theme.color.WHITE)
    m.errorMessage = styled("errorMessage", theme.textStyle.ERROR_MESSAGE, theme.color.WHITE)
    for each label in [m.errorTitle, m.errorMessage]
        label.width = ERROR_WIDTH
        label.translation = [(1920 - ERROR_WIDTH) \ 2, 0]
    end for
    m.retryButton = m.top.findNode("retryButton")
    m.tryAnywayButton = m.top.findNode("tryAnywayButton")
    m.tryAnywayButton.text = i18n.text("player.tryAnyway")
    m.backButton = m.top.findNode("backButton")
    m.backButton.text = i18n.text("player.goBack")
    for each button in [m.retryButton, m.tryAnywayButton, m.backButton]
        button.setFields({ variant: "solid", height: ERROR_BUTTON_HEIGHT, padding: 18, minWidth: 140, textStyle: theme.textStyle.ERROR_BUTTON })
    end for
    m.progressTimer = m.top.findNode("progressTimer")
    m.progressTimer.observeField("fire", "onProgressTimer")
    m.wakeTimer = m.top.findNode("wakeTimer")
    m.wakeTimer.observeField("fire", "onWakeTimer")
    m.controlsTimer = m.top.findNode("controlsTimer")
    m.controlsTimer.observeField("fire", "onControlsTimer")
    m.preferencesTimer = m.top.findNode("preferencesTimer")
    m.preferencesTimer.duration = PREFERENCES_WAIT_MS / 1000
    m.preferencesTimer.observeField("fire", "onPreferencesTimer")
    m.panelTimer = m.top.findNode("panelTimer")
    m.panelTimer.observeField("fire", "onPanelTimer")

    m.clock = CreateObject("roTimespan")
    ' The reducer's clocks and identity source (playback.session).
    m.env = {
        clock: m.clock,
        wallClock: CreateObject("roDateTime"),
        now: function() as Dynamic
            return m.clock.TotalMilliseconds()
        end function,
        epoch: function() as Dynamic
            m.wallClock.Mark()
            return m.wallClock.AsSeconds()
        end function,
        uuid: function() as String
            return CreateObject("roDeviceInfo").GetRandomUUID()
        end function
    }
    m.slot = playback.slot.create()
    ' Started with the first sidecar.
    m.mediaTask = invalid
    m.mediaQueue = []
    m.awaitedMediaTask = invalid

    ' What each pending request's answer is for, by request ID.
    m.requests = {}
    m.events = []
    m.dispatching = false
    m.state = invalid
    m.intent = invalid
    ' The content ID playing (onShow, then each next episode), and a next
    ' episode's season as Up Next found it, until its watch projection
    ' arrives (playingSeason).
    m.itemId = ""
    m.itemSeason = -1
    ' The watch projection, and the version of the file the plan plays
    ' (playback.intent.versionOf).
    m.watch = invalid
    m.version = invalid
    ' The entry's nav.player intent, when it has one, and Detail's track
    ' picks for the version the start plays (nav.player.tracksFor).
    m.wanted = invalid
    m.picks = invalid
    ' The intent whose start waits for the preferences, and whether the
    ' session's first plan is still to come (playback.options.afterStart).
    m.waiting = invalid
    m.firstPlan = true
    m.identity = invalid
    ' The last load number of the sessions before, for the next one's
    ' (playback.session.create).
    m.loads = 0
    ' The newest load: { load, plan, playStart, autoplay, reopen, fields,
    ' proxy, headersReady, assigned, sidecars, sidecarsAt }, and once
    ' assigned its content, the ready sidecars it carries (tracks), and the
    ' selected one's path (track), as the slot plays it.
    m.current = invalid
    ' The load whose content the Video node has, and whether it is a proxy's.
    m.activeLoad = invalid
    m.activeProxy = false
    ' Whether the active load's content has reached "playing"
    ' (playback.video.stateEvent), and its sidecar track's path.
    m.activePlayed = false
    m.activeTrack = ""
    ' Whether the plan's subtitle is one Roku must not draw
    ' (playback.sidecars.suppressed); the shown controls hide captions too
    ' (drawCaptions).
    m.subtitleSuppressed = false
    ' An in-place subtitle switch to check: { load, path, at } (checkSubtitle).
    m.subtitleCheck = invalid
    ' Whether the active content has started (the node left its stopped
    ' state for it), until when after its first frame the player makes no
    ' subtitle selection on its own (holdsSubtitle), whether the check after
    ' that has run, when to look again after its selection (confirmSubtitle),
    ' and when the player last changed the started content (noteWrite).
    m.activeStarted = false
    m.settleUntil = invalid
    m.subtitleConfirmed = false
    m.recheckAt = invalid
    m.wroteAt = invalid
    ' The subtitle selected (its track ID, "" for none) when content last
    ' finished right after the player changed it, and how many times in a
    ' row that happened with it selected; a viewer's track choice clears it.
    m.writeStops = { trackId: "", count: 0 }
    m.captionMode = ""
    m.videoMode = ""
    m.pauseLoad = invalid
    m.subtitleHandle = invalid
    m.headerGeneration = invalid
    m.flags = newFlags()
    ' The notice's time on the status line (playback.player.noticeShows).
    m.noticeClock = playback.player.newNoticeClock(0)
    ' The controls reducer, the events raised while its commands run, and
    ' whether focus waits for them (setOverlayFlags).
    m.controls = playback.controls.create()
    m.controlEvents = []
    m.controlsBusy = false
    m.refocus = false
    ' Read once per session, beside the watch projection.
    m.preferences = playback.preferences.defaults()
    m.preferencesRequested = false
    m.preferencesRead = false
    ' Auto-play next for Up Next: the profile's until the viewer changes it
    ' in Options or on the panel, which writes it for this device.
    m.autoplayNext = m.preferences.autoPlayNext
    m.autoplayChosen = false
    ' The Options panel while it is open, its copy, and the model it was
    ' last given, as JSON.
    m.optionsPanel = invalid
    m.optionsCopy = invalid
    m.optionsModel = ""
    ' The tab Options showed last, which it opens on next.
    m.optionsTab = playback.options.TAB_INFO
    m.modelType = CreateObject("roDeviceInfo").GetModelType()
    ' Roku's * overlay as the player watches it (playback.options.watchOverlay).
    m.overlayWatch = { played: false, audio: "", subtitle: "" }
    ' The seek previews' latest manifest read, and the file they are for.
    m.previewFetch = invalid
    m.previewFileId = ""
    ' Replay forced captions on over "Instant replay" (replayCaptions).
    m.replayForced = false
    ' The mode before Silo's last caption-mode write and until when Roku's
    ' first event may still repeat it (onPlatform).
    m.staleCaption = invalid
    ' The burned-in subtitle captions Off set aside, for On to ask for again,
    ' and the caption mode a plan's arrival last sent a track_change for
    ' (followCaptions).
    m.burnWanted = invalid
    m.followedMode = invalid
    ' The playing file's markers (playback.markers) and the file they are
    ' for; Skip Intro's and Up Next's reducers, Up Next's panel while it
    ' shows, the next episode's resolution and On Deck's read until they
    ' settle.
    m.markers = []
    m.markersFileId = ""
    m.skip = invalid
    m.recap = invalid
    m.upNext = invalid
    m.upNextPanel = invalid
    m.resolution = invalid
    m.onDeck = invalid
    ' The item's video played to its end (endOfVideo).
    m.videoEnded = false
    ' Up Next's next start ({ itemId, carry, seasonNumber, auto, replay,
    ' foreign }) until the session it ends is done.
    m.advance = invalid
    ' The chain moved on from the first item's title to an On Deck item:
    ' the entry's page is told no more (notePlayed).
    m.leftSeries = false
    m.errorVisible = false
    m.retryable = false
    ' The error says the server could not be reached: Try Anyway shows, and
    ' Retry checks the server first.
    m.unreachable = false
    m.checkingServer = false
    m.leaving = false
    m.done = false
    m.closed = false
    m.released = false
    m.slowStops = 0
    m.lastStopMs = invalid
end sub

function newFlags() as Object
    return { starting: false, stopping: false, reconnecting: false, progressPending: false, subtitlesLoading: false, notice: "" }
end function

function styled(id as String, style as String, color as String) as Object
    label = m.top.findNode(id)
    label.font = theme.font(style)
    label.color = color
    return label
end function

' --- Screen hooks -------------------------------------------------------------

sub onShow(event as Object)
    applyFocus()
    if not event.first then return
    params = m.top.entry.params
    m.itemId = ""
    m.startOver = false
    ' A deep link's or detail page's entry carries an intent
    ' (source/nav/player.bs); the test player entry passes the item ID and
    ' Start over directly.
    m.wanted = nav.player.intentOf(params)
    if m.wanted <> invalid
        m.itemId = m.wanted.contentId
        m.startOver = m.wanted.startPositionRule = nav.player.START_OVER
    else if util.isObject(params)
        m.itemId = util.text(params.itemId)
        m.startOver = util.isTrue(params.startOver)
    end if
    if m.itemId = ""
        showLocalError({ title: "Nothing to play", message: "No title was chosen." }, false)
        return
    end if
    loadWatch()
    ' A phone's profile handoff (docs/silocontrol.md section 4.2).
    if util.isObject(params) and util.text(params.profileName) <> ""
        line = "Playing as " + params.profileName
        if util.text(params.controller) <> "" then line = line + " · From " + params.controller
        notice(line)
    end if
end sub

' AppScene is destroying the screen: after this player finished, or for a new
' account, profile, or server. The reducer hands its stop to ApiTask first; a
' start still unanswered is ApiTask's to stop once AppScene releases this
' screen's owner (playback.worker.cancel).
sub onRelease()
    m.released = true
    if m.state <> invalid and not m.done
        if identityChanged()
            dispatch({ type: "identityChange" })
        else
            dispatch({ type: "back" })
        end if
    end if
    m.closed = true
    m.progressTimer.control = "stop"
    m.wakeTimer.control = "stop"
    m.controlsTimer.control = "stop"
    m.preferencesTimer.control = "stop"
    m.panelTimer.control = "stop"
    replayCaptions(false)
    m.video.control = "stop"
    ' MediaTask deletes the cache's files before it ends.
    trimCache(sidecarCache(), playback.sidecarCache.MAX_BYTES)
    stopMediaTask()
    ' AppScene releases the owner, and with it the manifest read.
    playback.trickplay.cancel(m.previewFetch)
    m.preview.active = false
    m.preview.manifest = {}
end sub

function identityChanged() as Boolean
    view = api.session.current()
    if view = invalid then return true
    ' A phone's borrowed identity (docs/silocontrol.md section 8.3).
    if nav.player.identityOf(m.top.entry.params) <> invalid
        borrowed = view.borrowed
        return not util.isObject(borrowed) or view.origin <> m.identity.server or borrowed.accountId <> m.identity.account or borrowed.profileId <> m.identity.profile
    end if
    if not util.isObject(view.profile) then return true
    return view.origin <> m.identity.server or view.accountId <> m.identity.account or view.profile.id <> m.identity.profile
end function

' --- Starting -------------------------------------------------------------------

' GET /api/v2/watch/{id}: the file, its audio tracks, and the saved position.
sub loadWatch()
    hideError()
    view = api.session.current()
    if view = invalid or view.status <> "signed_in" or not util.isObject(view.profile)
        showLocalError({ title: "Sign in first", message: "Sign in and choose a profile, then play again." }, false)
        return
    end if
    m.flags.starting = true
    handle = handleFor("onWatch")
    m.requests[api.send({ path: "/api/v2/watch/" + api.request.escape(m.itemId), auth: "profile" }, handle)] = "watch"
    loadPreferences()
    refreshChrome()
end sub

' The profile's playback preferences, once per session and in parallel with
' the watch projection: the start never waits for them, and the defaults
' apply until they answer or when the read fails.
sub loadPreferences()
    if m.preferencesRequested then return
    m.preferencesRequested = true
    m.requests[api.send(playback.preferences.request(), handleFor("onPreferences"))] = "preferences"
end sub

sub onPreferences(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    takeRequest(handle)
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    body = invalid
    if result <> invalid and result.ok = true
        body = result.body
    else
        status = 0
        if result <> invalid then status = result.status
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the playback preferences could not be read; using the defaults", { status: status })
    end if
    m.preferences = playback.preferences.parse(body)
    m.preferencesRead = true
    if not m.autoplayChosen then setAutoplay(m.preferences.autoPlayNext)
    runUpNext({ type: "prompt", seconds: m.preferences.nextUpPromptSeconds })
    if m.skip <> invalid and playback.skipIntro.modeOf(m.preferences.introSkipMode) <> m.skip.mode then runSkip({ type: "mode", mode: m.preferences.introSkipMode })
    runRecap({ type: "autoSkip", value: m.preferences.autoSkipRecap })
    m.overlay.skipBackSeconds = m.preferences.skipBackSeconds
    m.overlay.skipForwardSeconds = m.preferences.skipForwardSeconds
    dispatchControls({ type: "preferences", skipBackSeconds: m.preferences.skipBackSeconds, skipForwardSeconds: m.preferences.skipForwardSeconds })
    if m.waiting <> invalid then beginWaiting()
end sub

' The preferences are late: the start goes ahead with the defaults.
sub onPreferencesTimer()
    if m.waiting = invalid or m.closed then return
    log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the playback preferences are late; starting with the defaults", { ms: PREFERENCES_WAIT_MS })
    beginWaiting()
end sub

sub beginWaiting()
    intent = m.waiting
    m.waiting = invalid
    m.preferencesTimer.control = "stop"
    begin(intent)
end sub

sub onWatch(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    takeRequest(handle)
    ' Back while the next episode's projection was read.
    if m.leaving then return
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true
        status = 0
        if result <> invalid then status = result.status
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the item could not be read", { status: status })
        m.flags.starting = false
        if status = 404
            showLocalError({ title: "Not available", message: "This title is no longer available on the server." }, false)
        else
            showLocalError({ title: "Can't load this title", message: "Check the connection to the server, then try again." }, true)
        end if
        return
    end if
    ' The version Detail's Version button chose, else the start path's.
    intent = playback.intent.fromWatch(result.body, m.itemId, nav.player.pinnedFile(m.wanted))
    if intent = invalid
        m.flags.starting = false
        showLocalError({ title: "Can't play this title", message: "The server lists no file for it." }, false)
        return
    end if
    m.watch = result.body
    if m.preferencesRead
        begin(intent)
    else
        m.waiting = intent
        m.preferencesTimer.control = "start"
    end if
end sub

' Resume starts 7 s before the saved position, Start Over at 0, and a title
' never started where the server says. Up Next's next item resumes the same
' way, with the carry of the item before, and is an autoplay start unless
' the viewer chose it from On Deck.
sub begin(intent as Object)
    m.intent = intent
    m.version = playback.intent.versionOf(m.watch, intent.fileId)
    title = intent.name
    if title = "" then title = intent.title
    m.overlay.setFields({ series: playback.controls.seriesLine(intent), title: title, tag: playback.controls.episodeTag(intent) })
    carry = nav.player.carryOf(m.wanted)
    chained = carry <> invalid
    if chained
        ' The page the first episode was played from selects this one when
        ' the player leaves.
        if not m.leftSeries then nav.notePlayed(m.itemId, playingSeason())
        if util.isBoolean(carry.autoPlay)
            m.autoplayChosen = true
            setAutoplay(carry.autoPlay)
        end if
    end if
    readMarkers(intent.fileId)
    m.skip = playback.skipIntro.create(m.preferences.introSkipMode, m.markers)
    m.recap = playback.skipRecap.create(m.preferences.autoSkipRecap, m.markers)
    if not chained then carry = playback.upNext.newCarry()
    m.upNext = playback.upNext.create({ promptSeconds: m.preferences.nextUpPromptSeconds, runtime: intent.runtime, lookup: intent.kind = "episode", autoPlayNext: m.autoplayNext, deviceAutoplay: CreateObject("roDeviceInfo").IsAutoplayEnabled(), carry: carry })
    ' The Up Next button waits for the first plan (resolveNext).
    showUpNextButton(false)
    ' A phone's launch may play as its own profile, borrowed for this
    ' player (AppScene fences the player's requests to it).
    m.identity = nav.player.identityOf(m.top.entry.params)
    if m.identity = invalid
        view = api.session.current()
        m.identity = { server: view.origin, account: view.accountId, profile: view.profile.id }
    end if
    m.state = playback.session.create({ identity: m.identity, loads: m.loads })
    current = platform.current()
    m.captionMode = util.text(current.captionMode)
    m.preview.tier = playback.trickplay.previewTier(current.memory)
    ' A scrub before the first plan shows the time alone.
    m.preview.manifest = playback.trickplay.pending()
    platform.subscribe(m.top.owner, [platform.topic.CAPTION_MODE, platform.topic.MEMORY_LEVEL, platform.topic.CODEC_CAPABILITY, platform.topic.HDMI], "onPlatform")
    ' Hidden screens release their browse textures before any stream loads.
    platform.beforePlayback()
    startPosition = playback.intent.resumeAt(intent.resumeSeconds)
    if m.startOver then startPosition = 0
    ' A phone's launch names its own position (nav.player.startAt).
    phoneStart = nav.player.startSecondsOf(m.wanted)
    if util.isNumber(phoneStart) then startPosition = phoneStart
    m.progressTimer.control = "start"
    dispatchControls({ type: "show" })
    ' Detail's Audio and Subtitles choices for the version it read, else the
    ' worker's audio (the version's effective track) and no subtitle.
    m.picks = nav.player.tracksFor(m.wanted, intent.fileId)
    initial = playback.options.initialTracks(m.watch, m.preferences, m.picks)
    playIntent = { contentId: m.itemId, fileId: intent.fileId, pinsVersion: intent.pinned, audioTracks: intent.audioTracks, effectiveAudioIndex: intent.effectiveAudioIndex, versions: intent.versions, audioIndex: initial.audioIndex, subtitleIndex: initial.subtitleIndex, audioLanguage: util.text(m.preferences.audioLanguage) }
    ' The profile's quality and bitrate cap, as read before the start or the
    ' defaults (Auto, no cap); an Options choice replaces the quality for
    ' this title's session.
    dispatch({ type: "play", intent: playIntent, quality: m.preferences.preferredQuality, bandwidthCapKbps: m.preferences.maxBitrateKbps, autoplay: nav.player.isAutoStart(m.wanted), catalogRuntime: intent.runtime, startPosition: startPosition })
end sub

' --- The reducer ----------------------------------------------------------------

' Reduces event, and any event raised while its commands run, in order.
sub dispatch(event as Object)
    if m.state = invalid then return
    m.events.Push(event)
    if m.dispatching then return
    m.dispatching = true
    while m.events.Count() > 0 and not m.closed
        for each command in playback.session.reduce(m.state, m.events.Shift(), m.env)
            execute(command)
        end for
    end while
    m.events = []
    m.dispatching = false
    if m.closed then return
    scheduleWake()
    refreshChrome()
    advanceWhenDone()
end sub

sub execute(command as Object)
    t = command.type
    if t = "start"
        m.flags.starting = true
        m.requests[api.playback.start(command, handleFor("onCommandAnswer"))] = command
    else if t = "replan"
        m.requests[api.playback.replan(command, m.intent.audioTracks, handleFor("onCommandAnswer"))] = command
    else if t = "progress"
        m.requests[api.playback.progress(command, handleFor("onCommandAnswer"))] = command
    else if t = "routeEvent"
        api.playback.routeEvent(command, api.newHandle(m.top.owner))
    else if t = "job"
        api.playback.job(command, api.newHandle(m.top.owner))
    else if t = "load"
        m.flags.starting = false
        prepare({ load: command.load, plan: command.plan, playStart: command.playerStart, autoplay: command.autoplay, reopen: false, refresh: util.isTrue(command.refresh) })
        planLoaded(command.plan)
    else if t = "reopen"
        if m.current <> invalid then prepare({ load: command.load, plan: m.current.plan, playStart: command.playerPosition, autoplay: command.autoplay, reopen: true, refresh: util.isTrue(command.refresh), sidecars: m.current.sidecars, sidecarsAt: m.current.sidecarsAt })
    else if t = "retrack"
        retrack(command)
    else if t = "seek"
        seekLoad(command.load, command.playerPosition)
    else if t = "refuseAudioCodec"
        api.playback.refuseAudioCodec(command.codec, api.newHandle(m.top.owner))
    else if t = "reconnecting"
        m.flags.reconnecting = command.active
    else if t = "progressPending"
        m.flags.progressPending = command.pending
    else if t = "error"
        showReducerError(command, util.isTrue(command.retryable))
    else if t = "finished"
        endOfVideo()
    else if t = "exit"
        ' Up Next's next episode follows the session it ends.
        if m.advance = invalid then leavePlayer()
    else if t = "done"
        m.done = true
        closeWhenStopped()
    else if t = "log"
        if command.level = "debug"
            log.debug(LOG_TAG, command.message, command.fields)
        else if command.level = "info"
            log.info(LOG_TAG, command.message, command.fields)
        else
            log.warn(LOG_TAG, command.message, command.fields)
        end if
    else if t = "refused"
        refused(command.operation)
    end if
    ' "subtitleShift" needs nothing more: every plan's sidecar is fetched and
    ' shifted for its own timeline offset when the plan loads.
end sub

' The server refused a replan the session asked for, and the plan playing
' stays: a notice says a track or quality change did not happen. An
' output change follows the device, never the viewer, so it says nothing;
' Auto's own step down never comes here (playback.session).
sub refused(operation as String)
    if operation = "track_change"
        notice(i18n.text("player.trackRefused"))
    else if operation = "quality_change"
        notice(i18n.text("player.qualityRefused"))
    end if
end sub

' ApiTask's answer to a start, replan, or progress command.
sub onCommandAnswer(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    command = takeRequest(handle)
    if command = invalid then return
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    body = invalid
    if result <> invalid and result.ok = true then body = result.body
    if command.type = "start" and util.isObject(body) and util.text(body.reason) <> "" then log.warn(LOG_TAG, "start refused", { reason: body.reason })
    reducerEvent = playback.player.answerEvent(command, body)
    if reducerEvent <> invalid then dispatch(reducerEvent)
end sub

sub onProgressTimer()
    dispatch({ type: "tick" })
end sub

sub onWakeTimer()
    runSlot(playback.slot.tick(m.slot, m.env.now()))
    if m.current <> invalid then tryAssign(m.current)
    dispatch({ type: "wake" })
end sub

' The reducer's next wake, the slot's deadlines, or the end of the wait for
' sidecars, whichever comes first.
sub scheduleWake()
    now = m.env.now()
    wake = playback.session.nextWake(m.state, now, m.env.epoch())
    wake = sooner(wake, playback.slot.wakeAt(m.slot))
    item = m.current
    if item <> invalid and not item.assigned then wake = sooner(wake, playback.sidecars.waitUntil(item.sidecars, item.sidecarsAt))
    m.wakeTimer.control = "stop"
    if wake = invalid then return
    delay = (wake - now) / 1000
    if delay < 0.01 then delay = 0.01
    m.wakeTimer.duration = delay
    m.wakeTimer.control = "start"
end sub

function sooner(current as Dynamic, candidate as Dynamic) as Dynamic
    if candidate = invalid then return current
    if current = invalid or candidate < current then return candidate
    return current
end function

' --- Loads ------------------------------------------------------------------------

' A new plan's content: Options describes the file it plays, the previews
' and markers follow that file, and the session's first plan takes the
' subtitle the start's rule asks for (playback.options.afterStart), the
' preferences read as they are now; that is at most one track_change, and it
' leaves Roku's caption mode alone (assumption AG-75). With captions off, a
' subtitle only a burn-in would show is set aside for On instead. Any other
' plan may need to follow the caption mode (followCaptions). The first plan
' also starts Up Next's reads: the next episode's resolution and On Deck.
sub planLoaded(plan as Object)
    fileId = playback.intent.playingFile(plan, m.intent.fileId)
    m.version = playback.intent.versionOf(m.watch, fileId)
    followPreviews(fileId)
    followMarkers(fileId)
    change = invalid
    if m.firstPlan
        m.firstPlan = false
        resolveNext()
        change = playback.options.afterStart(plan, m.version, playback.options.initialTracks(m.watch, m.preferences, m.picks))
        if change <> invalid and m.captionMode = playback.options.CAPTION_OFF and playback.options.burnsIn(plan, change.tracks)
            m.burnWanted = change.tracks.subtitle
            change = invalid
        end if
    end if
    if change <> invalid
        dispatch(change)
    else
        followCaptions(true)
    end if
end sub

' A plan to play, or the current plan to reopen at a position: its content
' needs media headers for its URL (none for a proxy node), from refreshed
' tokens when the load renews the content's credential (refresh), and waits
' briefly for its subtitle sidecars, which a reopen keeps.
sub prepare(item as Object)
    if not item.reopen
        cancelSubtitle()
        item.sidecars = []
    end if
    m.current = item
    item.assigned = false
    item.headersReady = false
    base = serverBase()
    item.fields = playback.media.contentFields(item.plan, base, item.playStart, m.intent.title)
    if item.fields = invalid
        stream = item.plan.stream
        message = "unsupported stream"
        if util.isObject(stream) then message = message + " " + util.text(stream.protocol) + "/" + util.text(stream.container)
        dispatch({ type: "failure", load: item.load, kind: "player", message: message })
        return
    end if
    item.proxy = playback.media.isProxy(item.fields.url, base)
    if not item.reopen then log.info(LOG_TAG, "plan", playback.player.planFacts(item.plan, item.proxy))
    if not item.autoplay then m.pauseLoad = item.load
    if not item.reopen then startSidecars(item)
    ' A renewal refreshes the tokens first, unless they already were.
    m.requests[api.session.mediaHeaders(item.fields.url, m.headerGeneration, util.isTrue(item.refresh), handleFor("onHeaders"))] = item
end sub

sub onHeaders(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    item = takeRequest(handle)
    if item = invalid or not isCurrent(item.load) then return
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true
        reason = "media_headers"
        if result <> invalid and util.isObject(result.error) then reason = util.text(result.error.kind)
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "no media headers", { kind: reason })
        dispatch({ type: "unplayable", reason: reason })
        return
    end if
    item.headers = result.body.httpHeaders
    item.headersReady = true
    if util.isTrue(result.body.credentialed)
        m.headerGeneration = result.body.generation
        ' When the content's credential expires, and when to renew it.
        dispatch({ type: "credentials", load: item.load, expiresAt: result.body.expiresAt, renewFrom: result.body.refreshAt })
    end if
    tryAssign(item)
end sub

' Builds the item's content once its headers are in and its sidecars are
' ready, failed, or past their wait, and hands it to the slot. The content
' carries every ready sidecar, so the viewer can switch between them in
' place (playback.sidecars), but none for a plan without a subtitle once
' captions have come on (playback.sidecars.mayCarry).
sub tryAssign(item as Object)
    if item.assigned or not item.headersReady then return
    waitEnds = playback.sidecars.waitUntil(item.sidecars, item.sidecarsAt)
    if waitEnds <> invalid and m.env.now() < waitEnds
        if playback.sidecars.selectedPending(item.sidecars) then stopForSubtitle()
        return
    end if
    fields = item.fields
    content = CreateObject("roSGNode", "ContentNode")
    content.url = fields.url
    content.streamFormat = fields.streamFormat
    content.playStart = fields.playStart
    content.title = fields.title
    ' The lines exist only on this content node from here on.
    if item.headers.Count() > 0 then content.httpHeaders = item.headers
    item.headers = invalid
    item.content = content
    item.tracks = []
    item.track = ""
    if playback.sidecars.mayCarry(item.plan, m.captionMode)
        for each track in item.sidecars
            if track.state = "ready"
                item.tracks.Push(track)
                if track.selected then item.track = track.path
            end if
        end for
    end if
    if item.tracks.Count() > 0 then content.subtitleTracks = subtitleTracks(item.tracks)
    item.assigned = true
    runSlot(playback.slot.assign(m.slot, m.video.state, item, m.env.now()))
end sub

' While new content waits for its selected sidecar, the Video node plays
' nothing: the content before it, played on, would be played again from
' where the new plan starts, and stopped seconds later it may be stopping
' as Roku opens it (hardware run 24: 3.3-3.6 s, all after Roku listed the
' file's own tracks and before its first frame). The status line says
' "Loading subtitles…" meanwhile.
sub stopForSubtitle()
    if playback.slot.isStopping(m.slot) or playback.slot.isIdle(m.video.state) then return
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "the content waits for its subtitle; the Video node stops", invalid)
    runSlot(playback.slot.halt(m.slot, m.video.state, m.env.now()))
end sub

' --- Platform events --------------------------------------------------------

' The interface callback for platform.subscribe.
sub onPlatform(event as Object)
    if m.closed or m.state = invalid then return
    if event.type = platform.topic.CAPTION_MODE
        ' Roku's overlay changed it; Silo's UI writes it only on the
        ' viewer's choice (plan section 6.10), and Replay over "Instant
        ' replay" for its span, whose own write is not the viewer's.
        mode = util.text(event.mode)
        if m.replayForced and mode = "On" then return
        m.replayForced = false
        ' Roku's first event after Silo writes a mode sometimes repeats the
        ' mode before it (run 7: Instant replay before On mute; run 17: On or
        ' Instant replay before Off), so that one repeat is not the viewer's.
        stale = m.staleCaption
        m.staleCaption = invalid
        if stale <> invalid and mode = stale.mode and m.env.now() < stale.until then return
        ' The mode is Roku's setting, not what a Roku TV shows under On mute
        ' (platform.captionModeEvent), so muting and unmuting change nothing
        ' (hardware run 17). The echo of Silo's own write changes nothing.
        changed = mode <> m.captionMode
        m.captionMode = mode
        log.info(LOG_TAG, "caption mode", { mode: mode })
        refreshOptions()
        if changed then followCaptions(false)
        return
    end if
    if event.type = platform.topic.MEMORY_LEVEL
        m.preview.tier = playback.trickplay.previewTier(event)
        ' Under pressure the cache keeps only what plays.
        level = util.text(event.level)
        if level = memory.level.PRESSURE or level = memory.level.CRITICAL then trimCache(sidecarCache(), 0)
        return
    end if
    m.requests[api.playback.outputContext(handleFor("onOutputProbed"))] = "outputContext"
end sub

sub onOutputProbed(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    takeRequest(handle)
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true or not util.isObject(result.body) or not util.isString(result.body.outputContextId) then return
    dispatch({ type: "outputContext", outputContextId: result.body.outputContextId })
end sub

sub runSlot(actions as Object)
    for each action in actions
        if action.action = "stop"
            m.video.control = "stop"
        else if action.action = "play"
            playItem(action.item, action.waitedMs)
        else if action.action = "slow"
            m.slowStops = m.slowStops + 1
            log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the Video node is still stopping", { ms: playback.slot.FIRST_WAIT_MS })
        else if action.action = "stuck"
            log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the Video node did not stop", { ms: playback.slot.SECOND_WAIT_MS })
            if m.leaving
                closeWhenStopped()
            else
                dispatch({ type: "unplayable", reason: "video_stuck" })
            end if
        end if
    end for
end sub

' The caption mode is left as it is: only the viewer's choices in Silo's UI
' write it (plan section 6.10). Captions that came on while the content
' waited for the stop leave a plan without a subtitle no sidecars, and the
' node draws no subtitle but the plan's (playback.sidecars.suppressed).
sub playItem(item as Object, waitedMs as Dynamic)
    if waitedMs <> invalid
        m.lastStopMs = waitedMs
        log.info(LOG_TAG, "content assigned after the stop", { ms: waitedMs })
    end if
    ' An item that waited for the stop may have been replaced by a newer
    ' load, or the player may have left or shown an error meanwhile.
    if m.leaving or m.errorVisible or not isCurrent(item.load) then return
    if item.tracks.Count() > 0 and not playback.sidecars.mayCarry(item.plan, m.captionMode)
        item.tracks = []
        item.content.subtitleTracks = []
    end if
    m.activeLoad = item.load
    m.activeProxy = item.proxy
    m.activePlayed = false
    m.activeTrack = item.track
    m.subtitleCheck = invalid
    m.activeStarted = false
    m.settleUntil = invalid
    m.subtitleConfirmed = false
    m.recheckAt = invalid
    m.wroteAt = invalid
    m.subtitleSuppressed = playback.sidecars.suppressed(item.plan, item.track)
    drawCaptions()
    m.video.content = item.content
    if item.track <> "" then setSubtitleTrack(item.track)
    m.video.control = "play"
    ' The load's startup stall clock starts now (playback.session).
    dispatch({ type: "assigned", load: item.load })
end sub

' A local seek on the current plan, or, before its content plays, a later
' start position: on the fields while headers or the sidecar are awaited,
' on the content while it waits for the previous one to stop.
sub seekLoad(load as Integer, playerPosition as Dynamic)
    item = m.current
    if item = invalid or item.load <> load or item.fields = invalid then return
    if not item.assigned
        item.fields.playStart = playerPosition
    else if m.activeLoad <> invalid and m.activeLoad = load
        m.video.seek = playerPosition
    else
        item.content.playStart = playerPosition
    end if
end sub

function isCurrent(load as Integer) as Boolean
    return m.current <> invalid and m.current.load = load
end function

function serverBase() as String
    view = api.session.current()
    if view = invalid then return ""
    return util.text(view.origin)
end function

' --- Video callbacks ------------------------------------------------------------

sub onVideoState()
    videoState = m.video.state
    ' The state belongs to the content the node had; an idle state may let
    ' the slot assign newer content, which has reported nothing yet.
    load = m.activeLoad
    runSlot(playback.slot.stateChanged(m.slot, videoState, m.env.now()))
    if m.leaving
        closeWhenStopped()
        return
    end if
    if load = invalid or m.activeLoad <> load then return
    if videoState = "error"
        reportError(load)
        return
    end if
    if videoState = "buffering" or videoState = "playing" or videoState = "paused" then m.activeStarted = true
    firstFrame = false
    if videoState = "playing" and not m.activePlayed
        ' From here on, the node's tracks as they are now are the player's,
        ' and a change is the viewer's in Roku's overlay. Roku may still
        ' report a track it picked as the content opened; the player checks
        ' what Roku plays once the settle time is over (confirmSubtitle).
        m.overlayWatch.audio = util.text(m.video.audioTrack)
        m.overlayWatch.subtitle = util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack)
        m.activePlayed = true
        m.settleUntil = m.env.now() + SUBTITLE_SETTLE_MS
        logRokuSubtitle("first frame")
        firstFrame = true
        logFormats("first frame")
        ' Playback accepts remote keys: a deep-link launch fires AppLaunchComplete.
        m.top.ready = true
    end if
    if videoState = "playing" and m.pauseLoad <> invalid and m.pauseLoad = load
        ' A plan adopted while the viewer had paused opens paused.
        m.pauseLoad = invalid
        m.video.control = "pause"
    else if firstFrame
        ' The controls the start showed make way for the picture.
        dispatchControls({ type: "firstFrame" })
    end if
    afterWrite = false
    if videoState = "finished" and m.wroteAt <> invalid and m.state.plan <> invalid then afterWrite = m.env.now() - m.wroteAt <= WRITE_STOP_MS
    if afterWrite
        ' Roku stopped content right after the player changed it; the
        ' session reloads it unless it ended, and the reload's content
        ' carries the plan's selection (confirmSubtitle counts the stops).
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the Video node finished right after the player changed it", { played: m.activePlayed, ms: m.env.now() - m.wroteAt })
        trackId = playback.media.selectedSubtitle(m.state.plan.data)
        if trackId <> m.writeStops.trackId then m.writeStops = { trackId: trackId, count: 0 }
        m.writeStops.count = m.writeStops.count + 1
    end if
    reducerEvent = playback.video.stateEvent(videoState, load, m.activePlayed, afterWrite)
    if reducerEvent <> invalid
        dispatch(reducerEvent)
        runSkip({ type: "player", state: reducerEvent.state })
    end if
    ' The plan follows a caption mode that changed while its content loaded.
    if firstFrame then followCaptions(true)
    refreshChrome()
end sub

' What the device decodes, for Dolby Vision and audio checks on device runs
' (plan section 6.11): videoFormat has no Dolby Vision value, so the output
' mode is logged too.
sub logFormats(reason as String)
    m.videoMode = CreateObject("roDeviceInfo").GetVideoMode()
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "video formats", { reason: reason, videoFormat: util.text(m.video.videoFormat), audioFormat: util.text(m.video.audioFormat), videoMode: m.videoMode })
end sub

' errorStr can quote the media URL, and with it a signed token: it is
' redacted before it is logged or sent as the failure message.
sub reportError(load as Integer)
    detail = util.text(m.video.errorStr)
    message = "Video error " + util.text(m.video.errorCode) + ": " + redact.text(detail)
    failure = playback.video.failure(load, m.video.errorCode, m.video.errorInfo, detail, m.activeProxy, message)
    category = ""
    if util.isObject(m.video.errorInfo) then category = util.text(m.video.errorInfo.category)
    log.warn(LOG_TAG, "Video error", { error: m.video.errorCode, status: failure.status, category: category, kind: failure.event.kind, message: message })
    dispatch(failure.event)
end sub

' Skip Intro and Up Next follow the session's source position once the load
' plays.
sub onVideoPosition()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid then return
    dispatch({ type: "position", load: m.activeLoad, position: m.video.position })
    if m.state = invalid or m.state.plan = invalid or not m.state.plan.loadPlayed then return
    confirmSubtitle()
    checkSubtitle()
    position = m.state.player.position
    runSkip({ type: "position", seconds: position })
    runUpNext({ type: "position", seconds: position })
end sub

sub onVideoAudio()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid then return
    if m.activePlayed then logFormats("audio")
    reducerEvent = playback.video.audioEvent(m.video.audioFormat, m.activeLoad)
    if reducerEvent <> invalid then dispatch(reducerEvent)
end sub

sub onVideoFormat()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid or not m.activePlayed then return
    logFormats("video")
end sub

' Media data arrived. The stall clock tells a buffer that still fills (the
' network) from a decoder that has its media and shows nothing
' (playback.recovery.noteMedia). A segment whose download failed is not
' media.
sub onVideoSegment()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid then return
    reducerEvent = playback.video.segmentEvent(m.video.downloadedSegment, m.activeLoad)
    if reducerEvent <> invalid then dispatch(reducerEvent)
end sub

sub onVideoBuffer()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid then return
    reducerEvent = playback.video.bufferEvent(m.video.bufferingStatus, m.activeLoad)
    if reducerEvent <> invalid then dispatch(reducerEvent)
end sub

' Video.audioTrack or subtitleTrack changed. A track the viewer chose in
' Roku's * overlay becomes a track_change, or is written back when it is not
' one of the plan's (playback.options.watchOverlay, plan section 6.10). The
' node's values are read as they are now, so a queued callback sees the
' player's latest write; what Roku picks while content opens, and the echo
' of the player's own writes, are not choices.
sub onVideoTracks()
    if m.leaving or m.closed or m.state = invalid or m.state.plan = invalid or m.activeLoad = invalid then return
    logRokuSubtitle("track changed")
    watch = m.overlayWatch
    watch.played = m.activePlayed and isCurrent(m.activeLoad) and m.state.plan.load = m.activeLoad
    watch.version = m.version
    watch.rokuAudio = m.video.availableAudioTracks
    watch.contentTracks = invalid
    if watch.played then watch.contentTracks = m.current.tracks
    ' The audio is read first (playback.options.fromRokuOverlay).
    subtitle = util.text(m.video.audioTrack) = util.text(watch.audio)
    outcome = playback.options.watchOverlay(m.state.plan.data, watch, util.text(m.video.audioTrack), util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack))
    if outcome.kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_TRACKS
        log.info(LOG_TAG, "a track chosen in Roku's overlay", { inPlace: outcome.event.inPlace })
        trackChosen(subtitle)
        dispatch(outcome.event)
    else if outcome.kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_REVERT
        log.info(LOG_TAG, "a track chosen in Roku's overlay is not the plan's; it is put back", invalid)
        if outcome.DoesExist("audioTrack")
            noteWrite()
            m.video.audioTrack = outcome.audioTrack
        end if
        ' So soon after the first frame the change is Roku's, not the
        ' viewer's: the sidecar is selected once the content settles, if
        ' Roku still reports another track then (confirmSubtitle).
        if outcome.DoesExist("subtitleTrack") and not holdsSubtitle()
            noteWrite()
            setSubtitleTrack(outcome.subtitleTrack)
        end if
    end if
end sub

' --- Subtitles (plan section 6.8, transport 2) ------------------------------

' Downloads the sidecars the content carries (playback.sidecars.offered), one
' at a time and the plan's selected one first, each with the profile's
' credentials (all are on the configured origin); MediaTask then shifts and
' converts each to SRT. One the session's cache keeps is ready at once
' (playback.sidecarCache).
sub startSidecars(item as Object)
    offerSidecars(item, serverBase())
    fetchSidecar(item)
end sub

' The item's sidecars, against the server's base URL, those the cache keeps
' ready and the others queued.
sub offerSidecars(item as Object, base as String)
    item.sidecarsAt = m.env.now()
    cache = sidecarCache()
    selected = false
    for each track in playback.sidecars.offered(item.plan, base, m.captionMode)
        track.load = item.load
        track.state = "queued"
        track.path = playback.sidecarCache.take(cache, track.cacheKey)
        track.output = ""
        if track.path <> ""
            track.state = "ready"
            log.debug(LOG_TAG, "subtitle reused from this session", { format: track.format, selected: track.selected })
        else if track.selected
            m.flags.subtitlesLoading = true
        end if
        if track.selected then selected = true
        item.sidecars.Push(track)
    end for
    keepCache(cache)
    ' MediaTask looks for each kept file; one gone downloads again (keptGone).
    for each track in item.sidecars
        if track.state = "ready" then sendMedia({ id: item.load, track: track.trackId, kept: track.path })
    end for
    if playback.media.subtitleArtifact(item.plan) <> invalid and not selected then log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the subtitle sidecar is not on the configured origin", invalid)
end sub

' Starts the next queued sidecar's download while none is running.
sub fetchSidecar(item as Object)
    if m.subtitleHandle <> invalid then return
    for each track in item.sidecars
        if track.state = "queued"
            track.state = "loading"
            m.subtitleHandle = handleFor("onSubtitleDownloaded")
            m.requests[api.playback.subtitle(track.url, track.format, SUBTITLE_TIMEOUT_MS, m.subtitleHandle)] = track
            return
        end if
    end for
end sub

' A new plan replaces the sidecars still to come.
sub cancelSubtitle()
    m.flags.subtitlesLoading = false
    if m.subtitleHandle = invalid then return
    m.requests.Delete(m.subtitleHandle.requestId)
    api.cancel(m.subtitleHandle)
    m.subtitleHandle = invalid
end sub

sub onSubtitleDownloaded(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    track = takeRequest(handle)
    if m.subtitleHandle <> invalid and m.subtitleHandle.isSameNode(handle) then m.subtitleHandle = invalid
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if track = invalid or sidecarOf(track.load, track.trackId) = invalid
        if result <> invalid and result.ok = true then DeleteFile(result.body.path)
        return
    end if
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true
        kind = "network"
        if result <> invalid and util.isObject(result.error) then kind = util.text(result.error.kind)
        sidecarFailed(track, kind)
    else
        if track.cacheKey <> ""
            cache = sidecarCache()
            track.output = playback.sidecarCache.newPath(cache)
            keepCache(cache)
        end if
        sendMedia({ id: track.load, track: track.trackId, input: result.body.path, format: track.format, shiftSeconds: track.shiftSeconds, output: track.output, cacheKey: track.cacheKey })
    end if
    fetchSidecar(m.current)
end sub

' MediaTask takes requests once it observes its field, and starts once
' the one stopMediaTask retired has ended (mediaTaskRetiring).
sub sendMedia(request as Object)
    if m.mediaTask = invalid and not mediaTaskRetiring() then startMediaTask()
    if m.mediaTask <> invalid and m.mediaTask.ready
        m.mediaTask.request = request
    else
        m.mediaQueue.Push(request)
    end if
end sub

sub startMediaTask()
    m.mediaTask = CreateObject("roSGNode", "MediaTask")
    m.mediaTask.observeField("ready", "onMediaReady")
    m.mediaTask.observeField("result", "onMediaResult")
    m.mediaTask.control = "run"
end sub

' Whether the MediaTask stopMediaTask retired, this player's or an earlier
' one's, still runs. Its last requests delete files (clearOutputs, the
' cache's sweep) in the directories every MediaTask writes, so a
' replacement waits for it (onMediaTaskEnded).
function mediaTaskRetiring() as Boolean
    if not m.global.hasField("retiringMediaTask") then return false
    retiring = m.global.retiringMediaTask
    if retiring = invalid or retiring.state <> "run" then return false
    if m.awaitedMediaTask = invalid or not m.awaitedMediaTask.isSameNode(retiring)
        m.awaitedMediaTask = retiring
        retiring.observeField("state", "onMediaTaskEnded")
    end if
    return true
end function

' A closed player starts no MediaTask, which nothing would end.
sub onMediaTaskEnded()
    if m.closed or m.mediaTask <> invalid or m.mediaQueue.Count() = 0 or mediaTaskRetiring() then return
    m.awaitedMediaTask = invalid
    startMediaTask()
end sub

' MediaTask's callbacks may still arrive after stopMediaTask().
sub onMediaReady()
    if m.mediaTask = invalid or not m.mediaTask.ready then return
    for each request in m.mediaQueue
        m.mediaTask.request = request
    end for
    m.mediaQueue = []
end sub

sub onMediaResult(event as Object)
    result = event.getData()
    if not util.isObject(result) then return
    if cacheResult(result) then return
    if m.closed then return
    track = sidecarOf(result.id, result.track)
    if track = invalid then return
    if not util.isTrue(result.ok)
        sidecarFailed(track, util.text(result.error))
        return
    end if
    track.state = "ready"
    track.path = result.path
    if track.selected then m.flags.subtitlesLoading = false
    item = m.current
    if not item.assigned
        tryAssign(item)
    else if track.selected
        lateSubtitle(item, track)
    end if
    refreshChrome()
end sub

' --- The session's converted sidecars (playback.sidecarCache) ---------------------

' The index, in m.global, as it is now; keepCache puts back a changed one.
function sidecarCache() as Object
    if not m.global.hasField("sidecarCache") then m.global.addFields({ sidecarCache: playback.sidecarCache.create() })
    return m.global.sidecarCache
end function

sub keepCache(cache as Object)
    m.global.sidecarCache = cache
end sub

' Keeps a conversion MediaTask wrote for the cache, within its bound,
' whichever plan it was for. True for MediaTask's answer about a kept file
' (playback.sidecarFiles.check), which is the cache's alone.
function cacheResult(result as Object) as Boolean
    if result.DoesExist("kept")
        if util.isTrue(result.gone) then keptGone(result)
        return true
    end if
    if util.isTrue(result.ok) and util.text(result.cacheKey) <> ""
        cache = sidecarCache()
        playback.sidecarCache.put(cache, result.cacheKey, result.path, result.bytes)
        trimCache(cache, playback.sidecarCache.MAX_BYTES)
    end if
    return false
end function

' A kept file MediaTask found gone leaves the index, and a sidecar the
' current load offered from it downloads and converts again: content not
' built yet waits for it as for any other, and built content takes a
' selected one by the late path's reload (lateSubtitle).
sub keptGone(result as Object)
    cache = sidecarCache()
    playback.sidecarCache.forget(cache, result.kept)
    keepCache(cache)
    if m.closed then return
    track = sidecarOf(result.id, result.track)
    if track = invalid or track.path <> result.kept then return
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "the subtitle kept from this session is gone; it downloads again", { format: track.format, selected: track.selected })
    track.state = "queued"
    track.path = ""
    if track.selected then m.flags.subtitlesLoading = true
    fetchSidecar(m.current)
    refreshChrome()
end sub

' Brings the cache within limit bytes, keeping the files that content
' carries or that conversions still have to write; MediaTask deletes the
' others (playback.sidecarFiles.sweep). A closed player starts no
' MediaTask, which nothing would end; the next trim deletes them.
sub trimCache(cache as Object, limit as Integer)
    pinned = []
    content = m.video.content
    if content <> invalid and type(content.subtitleTracks) = "roArray"
        for each track in content.subtitleTracks
            pinned.Push(util.text(track.TrackName))
        end for
    end if
    if m.current <> invalid and type(m.current.sidecars) = "roArray"
        for each track in m.current.sidecars
            pinned.Push(util.text(track.path))
            pinned.Push(util.text(track.output))
        end for
    end if
    request = playback.sidecarCache.trim(cache, pinned, limit)
    keepCache(cache)
    if not m.closed or m.mediaTask <> invalid then sendMedia(request)
end sub

' A selected sidecar that arrives after its content was built. Content
' still waiting for the previous one to stop is not on the Video node yet
' and takes it. Content the node has never takes another track: Roku then
' listed only the added one and closed the player (hardware run 19). That
' content plays on without its subtitle, and the session reloads the plan
' at the position once nothing on its way replaces it; the new content
' carries the sidecar (playback.session's subtitleReady). A track change
' that comes first supersedes it.
sub lateSubtitle(item as Object, track as Object)
    if m.activeLoad = invalid or m.activeLoad <> item.load
        item.tracks.Push(track)
        item.track = track.path
        item.content.subtitleTracks = subtitleTracks(item.tracks)
        return
    end if
    tracks = invalid
    reload = playback.options.reloadSelection(item.plan)
    if reload <> invalid then tracks = reload.tracks
    dispatch({ type: "subtitleReady", load: item.load, tracks: tracks })
end sub

' Selects a sidecar on the playing content, or none, and lets Roku draw
' that and nothing else (playback.sidecars.suppressed). A sidecar is
' selected by the TrackName Roku lists for its path, or by the path until
' Roku lists the content's tracks (onVideoSubtitles), since Roku ignored a
' path it lists under another name (hardware run 17). Roku's overlay watch
' takes the name first, so the write's echo is no viewer's choice, then
' whatever the node holds after it.
sub selectSubtitle(path as String)
    noteWrite()
    m.subtitleSuppressed = playback.sidecars.suppressed(m.current.plan, path)
    drawCaptions()
    name = playback.sidecars.listedName(m.video.availableSubtitleTracks, path)
    if name = "" then name = path
    m.overlayWatch.subtitle = name
    setSubtitleTrack(name)
    m.overlayWatch.subtitle = util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack)
end sub

' Every write of Video.subtitleTrack, logged at debug level with its value:
' a TrackName Roku listed, the tmp:/ path the player gave it, or ""
' (hardware run 21's build could not show what the player had written).
sub setSubtitleTrack(name as String)
    log.debug(LOG_TAG, "subtitleTrack written", { value: trackLabel(name) })
    m.video.subtitleTrack = name
end sub

' What Roku reports about the active content's subtitle at debug level: the
' track selected (Video.subtitleTrack) and the one it plays
' (Video.currentSubtitleTrack).
sub logRokuSubtitle(reason as String)
    log.debug(LOG_TAG, "Roku's subtitle tracks", { reason: reason, selected: trackLabel(util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack)), playing: trackLabel(util.text(m.video.currentSubtitleTrack)) })
end sub

' A track name as it is logged: a listed TrackName, a tmp:/ path, or a
' track Roku found in the stream; a name with a URL in it is masked.
function trackLabel(name as String) as String
    if Instr(1, name, "://") > 0 then return redact.MASK
    return name
end function

' Once the active content has settled (SUBTITLE_SETTLE_MS after its first
' frame, holdsSubtitle), the player checks at the next position report
' whether Roku draws the plan's sidecar (playback.sidecars.drawn) and,
' when Roku reports another track, selects the sidecar by its listed
' name, once per load. Hardware run 21: after a reload with Arabic or
' Italian selected, Roku reported the sidecar selected but played the
' file's English track (mkv/3) or the English sidecar, and drew English
' while Options showed the choice. A stream track in the sidecar's
' language gets the selection too: in hardware run 22 Roku reported the
' file's only English track (mkv/4) playing for the English sidecar and
' drew nothing. A "finished" right after the write reloads the plan
' (noteWrite), and the reload's content is checked once again; after
' WRITE_STOPS_QUIET such stops in a row with the subtitle selected, the
' player selects it on its own no more until the viewer chooses a track. A
' track Roku still plays instead SUBTITLE_CHECK_MS after the write is
' logged and left. A viewer's switch before the check replaces it
' (retrack).
sub confirmSubtitle()
    if m.recheckAt <> invalid
        if m.env.now() < m.recheckAt then return
        m.recheckAt = invalid
        if not isCurrent(m.activeLoad) then return
        logRokuSubtitle("after the selection")
        if not subtitleDrawn() then log.info(LOG_TAG, "Roku still plays another subtitle track after the player selected the sidecar; left as it is", { playing: trackLabel(util.text(m.video.currentSubtitleTrack)) })
        return
    end if
    if m.subtitleConfirmed or m.settleUntil = invalid or holdsSubtitle() then return
    m.subtitleConfirmed = true
    path = m.activeTrack
    if path = "" or not isCurrent(m.activeLoad) then return
    logRokuSubtitle("settled")
    if subtitleDrawn() then return
    playing = trackLabel(util.text(m.video.currentSubtitleTrack))
    if m.writeStops.count >= WRITE_STOPS_QUIET and m.writeStops.trackId = playback.media.selectedSubtitle(m.state.plan.data)
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the sidecar is not selected again after Roku stopped its content twice", { playing: playing })
        return
    end if
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "Roku plays another subtitle track once the content settled; the sidecar is selected", { playing: playing })
    selectSubtitle(path)
    m.recheckAt = m.env.now() + SUBTITLE_CHECK_MS
end sub

function subtitleDrawn() as Boolean
    return playback.sidecars.drawn(m.activeTrack, util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack), util.text(m.video.currentSubtitleTrack))
end function

' Whether the active content takes no subtitle selection the player makes
' on its own: from its start until SUBTITLE_SETTLE_MS after its first frame
' (hardware run 20). Before it starts, the content is still being set up.
function holdsSubtitle() as Boolean
    if not m.activeStarted then return false
    return not m.activePlayed or m.env.now() < m.settleUntil
end function

' The player changes content the Video node has started (its subtitle,
' audio, caption drawing, or caption mode). A "finished" from it within
' WRITE_STOP_MS is the change's doing (onVideoState). Seeks are not
' counted: one may reach the content's end.
sub noteWrite()
    if m.activeStarted then m.wroteAt = m.env.now()
end sub

' Video.suppressCaptions: set for a subtitle Roku must not draw, and while
' the controls show. Roku draws captions above the UI at a place of its
' own, so a cue covered the scrubber and the time row (hardware run 26);
' tvOS draws its controls over its subtitles, and Roku hides them instead
' until the controls hide (assumption AG-293). The field is the node's
' own, which Roku documents for UI drawn where captions are; the caption
' mode is left alone. Content still settling (SUBTITLE_SETTLE_MS after its
' first frame) is not changed for it, as the player selects no subtitle on
' its own then (hardware run 20).
sub drawCaptions()
    covered = m.overlay.shown and not m.controls.upNext and m.settleUntil <> invalid and m.env.now() >= m.settleUntil
    suppressed = m.subtitleSuppressed or covered
    if suppressed = m.video.suppressCaptions then return
    noteWrite()
    m.video.suppressCaptions = suppressed
end sub

' Roku lists the tracks of the content it opens (Video.availableSubtitleTracks):
' the sidecars it carries, by TrackNames of Roku's own, and those Roku finds in
' the stream. While the content is set up, before it starts, the selected
' sidecar is selected by its listed name unless Roku reports it selected.
' From its start the player selects nothing on its own until it settles
' (holdsSubtitle, confirmSubtitle). Hardware run 20: on MKV originals, Roku
' reported subtitleTrack as the bare path after the player wrote the listed
' name; a second listing about 1 s in reported the file's own track (mkv/3)
' as currentSubtitleTrack; the player selected the sidecar again, and Roku
' stopped the content 0.17 s later, before any frame (4 of 5 loads), while
' a build that did not select again played 2 of 2 with cues.
sub onVideoSubtitles()
    if m.leaving or m.activeLoad = invalid or not isCurrent(m.activeLoad) then return
    listed = m.video.availableSubtitleTracks
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "Roku lists subtitle tracks", { tracks: listed })
    logRokuSubtitle("listed")
    path = m.activeTrack
    if m.activeStarted or playback.sidecars.listedName(listed, path) = "" or playback.sidecars.isTrack(util.text(m.video.subtitleTrack), path) then return
    selectSubtitle(path)
end sub

' Roku reports the track it plays (Video.currentSubtitleTrack, "the
' identifier of the subtitle track that is playing"). Once SUBTITLE_CHECK_MS
' have passed since an in-place switch, another sidecar of the content
' reported there, by any name that contains its path, means Roku kept the
' track it drew before (hardware run 17), so the plan's selection reloads,
' which draws it. Only once per switch, and never while content starts: a
' switch in place needs content that has played (playback.session's
' retrackRefusals), so its check comes after the settle time (holdsSubtitle). A
' track Roku found in the stream (hardware run 20's mkv/3) is not another
' sidecar and is only logged. While another track change is on its way the
' check waits for it (W11-3): its plan checks its own selection (retrack)
' or loads new content, which ends the check, and a refusal leaves this one
' to the next report.
sub checkSubtitle()
    check = m.subtitleCheck
    if check = invalid or m.env.now() < check.at or playback.session.changingTracks(m.state) then return
    m.subtitleCheck = invalid
    if m.activeLoad <> check.load or not isCurrent(check.load) then return
    playing = util.text(m.video.currentSubtitleTrack)
    other = playback.sidecars.trackPath(m.current.tracks, playing)
    if other = check.path then return
    if other = ""
        if playing <> "" then log.info(LOG_TAG, "Roku reports a track of its own as playing after the switch; left as it is", { playing: playing })
        return
    end if
    reload = playback.options.reloadSelection(m.state.plan.data)
    if reload = invalid then return
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "Roku did not switch the subtitle in place; the plan reloads", invalid)
    dispatch(reload)
end sub

sub sidecarFailed(track as Object, kind as String)
    track.state = "failed"
    log.warn(LOG_TAG, "subtitles failed", { kind: kind, format: track.format, selected: track.selected })
    if track.selected
        m.flags.subtitlesLoading = false
        if kind = "too_large" or kind = "too_many_cues"
            notice("Subtitles are too large to show.")
        else
            notice("Subtitles are not available.")
        end if
    end if
    tryAssign(m.current)
    refreshChrome()
end sub

' A track_change answered with a plan for the same media
' (playback.session): the content plays on, from the URL it loaded with
' until the reducer reloads it into the plan's, and shows the plan's subtitle
' from the sidecars it carries, or none, with Roku's caption mode as the
' viewer's choice set it. Off clears Roku's selection too; if captions are
' on by then, the plan reloads without the carried tracks (followCaptions).
sub retrack(command as Object)
    item = m.current
    if item = invalid or item.load <> command.load or not item.assigned then return
    item.plan = command.plan
    selectedId = ""
    artifact = playback.media.subtitleArtifact(item.plan)
    if artifact <> invalid then selectedId = artifact.trackId
    for each track in item.sidecars
        track.selected = track.trackId = selectedId
    end for
    m.flags.subtitlesLoading = false
    path = playback.sidecars.pathOf(item.tracks, selectedId)
    if selectedId <> "" and path = ""
        ' The server chose a track the content does not carry.
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the plan's subtitle is not on the playing content", invalid)
        notice("Subtitles are not available.")
    end if
    item.track = path
    m.activeTrack = path
    ' The viewer's choice, made whenever it comes; its own check replaces
    ' the one after the content settles.
    selectSubtitle(path)
    m.subtitleConfirmed = true
    m.recheckAt = invalid
    m.subtitleCheck = invalid
    if path <> "" then m.subtitleCheck = { load: item.load, path: path, at: m.env.now() + SUBTITLE_CHECK_MS }
    followCaptions(true)
end sub

' Its tracks are deleted when the player stops (plan section 4.8); a Task
' that has not started yet clears what is left when the next one starts.
sub stopMediaTask()
    if m.mediaTask = invalid then return
    if m.mediaTask.ready
        m.mediaTask.request = { finish: true }
        if not m.global.hasField("retiringMediaTask") then m.global.addField("retiringMediaTask", "node", false)
        m.global.retiringMediaTask = m.mediaTask
    else
        m.mediaTask.control = "stop"
    end if
    m.mediaTask = invalid
end sub

' The current item's sidecar for this load and track, or invalid when the
' answer is about a plan since replaced.
function sidecarOf(load as Dynamic, trackId as Dynamic) as Dynamic
    if m.current = invalid then return invalid
    for each track in m.current.sidecars
        if track.load = load and track.trackId = trackId then return track
    end for
    return invalid
end function

' The content's SubtitleTracks, the selected sidecar first: Roku draws a
' track it picks by the caption language until it lists the content's tracks
' and the selected one is selected by its listed name (onVideoSubtitles).
function subtitleTracks(tracks as Object) as Object
    out = []
    for each track in tracks
        entry = { Language: track.language, TrackName: track.path, Description: track.label }
        if track.selected
            out.Unshift(entry)
        else
            out.Push(entry)
        end if
    end for
    return out
end function

' --- Leaving and errors -------------------------------------------------------------

' The reducer ended the session: stop the node, then close once the reducer
' is done and the node has stopped.
sub leavePlayer()
    if m.leaving then return
    notePlayedLast()
    closeOptionsPanel()
    m.leaving = true
    m.flags.stopping = true
    m.progressTimer.control = "stop"
    m.controlsTimer.control = "stop"
    m.panelTimer.control = "stop"
    cancelSubtitle()
    runSlot(playback.slot.halt(m.slot, m.video.state, m.env.now()))
    closeWhenStopped()
end sub

' Hands the page the player was opened from its last item and whether
' this playback finished it, before the player leaves, unless the chain
' moved on to another title (advanceWhenDone told it then).
sub notePlayedLast()
    if m.itemId = "" or m.leftSeries then return
    nav.notePlayed(m.itemId, playingSeason(), playback.upNext.leftFinished(m.upNext, m.videoEnded))
end sub

' The playing item's season number: its watch projection's, else, for a
' next episode left before that arrived, the season Up Next found it in;
' -1 when neither is known.
function playingSeason() as Integer
    if util.isObject(m.watch) and util.isNumber(m.watch.season_number) then return Int(m.watch.season_number)
    return m.itemSeason
end function

sub closeWhenStopped()
    if not m.leaving or not m.done or m.closed or m.released or playback.slot.isStopping(m.slot) then return
    m.closed = true
    ' AppScene releases this screen before pop returns.
    nav.pop()
end sub

' The reducer's error, with Retry when it allows one, and Try Anyway when
' the server could not be reached.
sub showReducerError(command as Object, retryable as Boolean)
    m.flags.starting = false
    runSlot(playback.slot.halt(m.slot, m.video.state, m.env.now()))
    m.activeLoad = invalid
    showLocalError(playback.player.errorCopy(command), retryable, util.isTrue(command.serverUnreachable))
end sub

' The full-screen error (spec section 5.7), centred as tvOS's: the warning
' triangle, the title and message, then Retry ("Try again" when the server
' could not be reached), Try Anyway for an unreachable server once a
' session exists, and Go Back; Go Back alone when nothing can be retried.
' The player keeps focus and highlights the buttons.
sub showLocalError(copy as Object, retryable as Boolean, unreachable = false as Boolean)
    closeOptionsPanel()
    ' Up Next closes as Keep Watching closes it; the end opens it again.
    if m.upNextPanel <> invalid then runUpNext({ type: "hide" })
    m.errorTitle.text = copy.title
    m.errorMessage.text = copy.message
    m.retryable = retryable
    m.unreachable = retryable and unreachable and m.state <> invalid
    m.checkingServer = false
    buttons = []
    if retryable
        m.retryButton.text = i18n.text("states.retry")
        if unreachable then m.retryButton.text = i18n.text("common.tryAgain")
        buttons.Push(m.retryButton)
        if m.unreachable then buttons.Push(m.tryAnywayButton)
    end if
    buttons.Push(m.backButton)
    m.retryButton.visible = retryable
    m.tryAnywayButton.visible = m.unreachable
    layoutError(buttons)
    setControlRows([buttons], true, [copy.title, copy.message])
    m.errorPanel.visible = true
    m.errorVisible = true
    dispatchControls({ type: "hide" })
    applyFocus()
    refreshChrome()
    ' The error screen is operable, so a deep-link launch still completes.
    m.top.ready = true
end sub

' Stacks the failure screen and centres it on the screen, the buttons in a
' centred row.
sub layoutError(buttons as Object)
    titleHeight = Int(m.errorTitle.boundingRect().height)
    messageHeight = Int(m.errorMessage.boundingRect().height)
    height = ERROR_ICON + ERROR_GAP + titleHeight + ERROR_LINE_GAP + messageHeight + ERROR_GAP + ERROR_BUTTON_HEIGHT
    y = (1080 - height) \ 2
    m.errorIcon.translation = [(1920 - ERROR_ICON) \ 2, y]
    y = y + ERROR_ICON + ERROR_GAP
    m.errorTitle.translation = [m.errorTitle.translation[0], y]
    y = y + titleHeight + ERROR_LINE_GAP
    m.errorMessage.translation = [m.errorMessage.translation[0], y]
    y = y + messageHeight + ERROR_GAP
    total = (buttons.Count() - 1) * ERROR_GAP
    for each button in buttons
        total = total + button.drawnWidth
    end for
    x = (1920 - total) \ 2
    for each button in buttons
        button.translation = [x, y]
        x = x + button.drawnWidth + ERROR_GAP
    end for
end sub

sub hideError()
    m.errorPanel.visible = false
    m.errorVisible = false
    m.unreachable = false
    m.checkingServer = false
    applyFocus()
end sub

sub errorAction(button as Dynamic)
    if button = invalid or m.checkingServer then return
    if not m.retryable or button.isSameNode(m.backButton)
        exitPlayer()
    else if button.isSameNode(m.tryAnywayButton)
        ' A new attempt at once, without the check (Android TV's force).
        hideError()
        dispatch({ type: "retry" })
    else if m.state = invalid
        hideError()
        loadWatch()
    else if m.unreachable
        ' Retry checks the server first, as Android TV does.
        m.checkingServer = true
        m.requests[api.send({ path: "/api/v2/system/info" }, handleFor("onServerChecked"))] = "serverCheck"
    else
        hideError()
        dispatch({ type: "retry" })
    end if
end sub

sub onServerChecked(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    takeRequest(handle)
    if not m.checkingServer then return
    m.checkingServer = false
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "the server is still unreachable", invalid)
        return
    end if
    hideError()
    dispatch({ type: "retry" })
end sub

' Back on the error screen or with nothing playing, the Close button, and
' the controls' exit: the reducer stops the session, then the player leaves.
' After the video's end the session has already stopped, and Up Next's
' advance has already asked it to stop: the player leaves instead of
' starting the next episode.
sub exitPlayer()
    if m.state = invalid
        if not m.leaving then notePlayedLast()
        m.leaving = true
        m.done = true
        closeWhenStopped()
    else if m.done or m.advance <> invalid
        m.advance = invalid
        leavePlayer()
    else
        dispatch({ type: "back" })
    end if
end sub

' --- Keys and the overlay ---------------------------------------------------------

function onKeyEvent(key as String, press as Boolean) as Boolean
    if m.leaving then return true
    if m.errorVisible
        if not press then return true
        if key = "back"
            exitPlayer()
        else if key = "OK"
            errorAction(highlightedControl())
        else
            moveHighlight(key)
        end if
        return true
    end if
    if Instr(1, CONTROL_KEYS, "|" + key + "|") = 0 then return false
    if key = "options" and press then logFocus("options key")
    if m.state = invalid
        ' Nothing plays yet: only Back does anything.
        if press and key = "back" then exitPlayer()
        return true
    end if
    dispatchControls({ type: "key", key: key, press: press })
    return true
end function

' The Video node while the controls hide, so * reaches Roku's overlay; the
' overlay's keyFocus while they show; the screen's anchor under the error. A
' panel that reported itself with setOverlayFlags keeps the focus it took.
sub applyFocus()
    c = m.controls
    if c.options or c.picker or c.upNext then return
    if m.errorVisible
        focusScreen()
    else if c.shown
        m.overlayFocus.setFocus(true)
    else
        m.video.setFocus(true)
    end if
end sub

' Which of the player's nodes has focus, logged in development builds
' only, for device runs: the coordinator's check at a417adb saw * with the
' controls shown open the Roku TV's Settings menu, which Roku shows only
' for a focused Video node. Cheap enough to work out in release builds,
' where log.debug prints nothing, on the rare calls it has.
sub logFocus(reason as String)
    log.debug(LOG_TAG, "focus", { reason: reason, focused: focusedName(), controls: m.controls.shown })
end sub

function focusedName() as String
    named = { video: m.video, keyFocus: m.overlayFocus, overlay: m.overlay, focusAnchor: m.top.findNode("focusAnchor"), player: m.top }
    for each name in named
        if named[name].hasFocus() then return name
    end for
    if m.optionsPanel <> invalid and m.optionsPanel.isInFocusChain() then return "optionsPanel"
    if m.upNextPanel <> invalid and m.upNextPanel.isInFocusChain() then return "upNextPanel"
    if m.top.isInFocusChain() then return "inside the player"
    return "outside the player"
end function

' Reduces event, and any event raised while its commands run, in order.
sub dispatchControls(event as Object)
    m.controlEvents.Push(event)
    if m.controlsBusy then return
    m.controlsBusy = true
    while m.controlEvents.Count() > 0 and not m.closed
        for each command in playback.controls.reduce(m.controls, m.controlEvents.Shift(), m.env.now())
            executeControl(command)
        end for
    end while
    m.controlEvents = []
    m.controlsBusy = false
    if m.closed then return
    if m.refocus
        m.refocus = false
        applyFocus()
    end if
    c = m.controls
    ' Options draws over the video alone: the controls step aside while it
    ' is open (tvOS), and come back with it closed.
    m.overlay.shown = c.shown and not c.options
    m.overlay.focusTarget = c.focus
    drawCaptions()
    restyleSkipPills()
    scrubbing = playback.controls.isScrubbing(c)
    ' Observers of scrubbing read scrubPosition, so it is set first.
    if scrubbing then m.overlay.scrubPosition = c.pending
    m.overlay.scrubbing = scrubbing
    m.overlay.rate = c.rate
    updatePreview()
    wake = playback.controls.nextWake(c)
    m.controlsTimer.control = "stop"
    if wake = invalid then return
    delay = (wake - m.env.now()) / 1000
    if delay < 0.01 then delay = 0.01
    m.controlsTimer.duration = delay
    m.controlsTimer.control = "start"
end sub

sub executeControl(command as Object)
    t = command.type
    if t = "visibility"
        applyFocus()
        if command.shown then logFocus("controls shown") else logFocus("controls hidden")
    else if t = "seek"
        commitSeek(command.position, util.isTrue(command.resume))
    else if t = "togglePause"
        togglePause()
    else if t = "openOptions"
        openOptions(command.tab)
    else if t = "openUpNext"
        openUpNext()
    else if t = "upNextBack"
        runUpNext({ type: "back" })
    else if t = "activateSkip"
        activateSkip()
    else if t = "activateRecap"
        runRecap({ type: "press" })
    else if t = "dismissSkip"
        dismissSkip()
    else if t = "closeOptions"
        closeOptionsPanel()
    else if t = "exit"
        exitPlayer()
    else if t = "replayCaptions"
        replayCaptions(command.active)
    end if
end sub

sub onControlsTimer()
    dispatchControls({ type: "wake" })
end sub

' The content a newer load is about to replace (a renewal's reload waiting
' for its headers) is left as it is: the new load opens as the session
' decided, and resuming the old content would play its old position until
' then (hardware run 9, T1e).
sub togglePause()
    if m.current <> invalid and m.activeLoad <> invalid and m.current.load <> m.activeLoad then return
    if m.video.state = "playing"
        m.video.control = "pause"
    else if m.video.state = "paused"
        m.video.control = "resume"
    end if
end sub

' In Roku's "Instant replay" caption mode, captions show from a Replay to
' where it was pressed, then the mode returns (plan section 6.10). The
' mode Silo writes comes back as a platform event, which onPlatform ignores
' while forced.
sub replayCaptions(active as Boolean)
    if active
        if m.replayForced or m.captionMode <> INSTANT_REPLAY then return
        m.replayForced = true
        noteWrite()
        m.video.globalCaptionMode = "On"
    else if m.replayForced
        m.replayForced = false
        noteWrite()
        m.video.globalCaptionMode = INSTANT_REPLAY
    end if
end sub

' --- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------

' Opens the Options panel on a tab (playback.options.TAB_*), or on the one
' it showed last in this player (playback.controls.LAST_TAB; Info the first
' time). It takes focus when its tab is set, after the controls reducer
' knows it is open.
sub openOptions(page as String)
    if m.optionsPanel <> invalid or m.state = invalid then return
    if page = playback.controls.LAST_TAB then page = m.optionsTab
    m.optionsPanel = m.optionsLayer.createChild("OptionsPanel")
    m.status.below = m.optionsPanel.bottom
    refreshOptions()
    m.optionsPanel.observeField("choice", "onOptionsChoice")
    m.optionsPanel.observeField("picker", "onOptionsPicker")
    m.optionsPanel.observeField("closed", "closeOptionsPanel")
    setOverlayFlags({ options: true })
    m.optionsPanel.tab = page
end sub

' What playback.options decides from, as its namespace comment lists it.
function optionsState() as Object
    plan = invalid
    if m.state.plan <> invalid then plan = m.state.plan.data
    item = m.current
    contentTracks = invalid
    if item <> invalid and item.assigned and m.activeLoad <> invalid and m.activeLoad = item.load then contentTracks = item.tracks
    overview = ""
    if util.isObject(m.watch) then overview = util.text(m.watch.overview)
    return {
        plan: plan,
        version: m.version,
        quality: m.state.quality,
        switching: switchingQuality(),
        captionMode: m.captionMode,
        modelType: m.modelType,
        autoplay: m.autoplayNext,
        episode: m.intent.kind = "episode",
        info: { series: m.overlay.series, title: m.overlay.title, tag: m.overlay.tag, year: m.intent.year, runtime: playback.options.runtimeText(m.intent.runtime, optionsWords().strings), overview: overview },
        stats: playback.player.statsColumns(plan, m.activeProxy, { videoFormat: m.video.videoFormat, audioFormat: m.video.audioFormat, videoMode: m.videoMode, captionMode: m.captionMode, slowStops: m.slowStops, lastStopMs: m.lastStopMs }),
        contentTracks: contentTracks,
        rokuSubtitles: m.video.availableSubtitleTracks,
        subtitleLanguage: playback.options.subtitleOrderLanguage(m.watch),
        burnWanted: m.burnWanted
    }
end function

' Whether a quality change is on its way: Options' Quality row reads
' "Switching…" and opens nothing meanwhile (tvOS ccf39a8b).
function switchingQuality() as Boolean
    if m.state.mutation <> invalid and m.state.mutation.request.op = "quality_change" then return true
    return m.state.queued <> invalid and m.state.queued.op = "quality_change"
end function

' Gives the open panel its model again when what it shows changed: a new
' plan or retrack, a choice, the caption mode, the content's sidecars, or
' the Stats text. An unchanged model is not set again, so the panel keeps
' its list as it is.
sub refreshOptions()
    if m.optionsPanel = invalid then return
    model = playback.options.model(optionsState(), optionsWords())
    text = FormatJson(model)
    if text = m.optionsModel then return
    m.optionsModel = text
    m.optionsPanel.model = model
end sub

' Options' copy (playback.options.words), read once.
function optionsWords() as Object
    if m.optionsCopy = invalid
        i18n.install()
        m.optionsCopy = playback.options.words(m.global.strings)
    end if
    return m.optionsCopy
end function

' A row the viewer chose (playback.options.choose): quality and track
' changes go through the session reducer; a caption mode, and On when a
' subtitle track is chosen with captions off, are written to Roku's caption
' mode, which a viewer's choice may change (assumption AG-75), and a mode
' alone may need a plan to follow it (followCaptions); Auto-play next is
' kept for this session.
sub onOptionsChoice()
    if m.optionsPanel = invalid or m.state = invalid then return
    applyChoice(m.optionsPanel.choice)
end sub

' A row's { kind, value }, from Options or a phone (PlayerRemote.bs).
sub applyChoice(choice as Object)
    outcome = playback.options.choose(optionsState(), choice)
    kind = outcome.kind
    ' A subtitle row is a choice even when it holds already (Off again).
    subtitle = util.text(choice.kind) = playback.options.KIND_SUBTITLE
    if subtitle or kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_TRACKS then trackChosen(subtitle)
    if kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_CAPTION
        setCaptionMode(outcome.captionMode)
        followCaptions(false)
    else if kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_TRACKS
        if outcome.captionMode <> invalid then setCaptionMode(outcome.captionMode)
        dispatch(outcome.event)
    else if kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_QUALITY
        dispatch(outcome.event)
    else if kind = playback.options.OUTCOME_AUTOPLAY
        chooseAutoplay(outcome.autoplay)
    end if
    refreshOptions()
end sub

' Focus entered or left the panel's list, its open picker.
sub onOptionsPicker()
    if m.optionsPanel <> invalid then setOverlayFlags({ picker: m.optionsPanel.picker })
end sub

' The panel closed, or Back reached the controls reducer while it was open,
' or an error or the player's exit covers it: it goes, and focus returns to
' the controls, or to the Video node while they hide.
sub closeOptionsPanel()
    panel = m.optionsPanel
    if panel = invalid then return
    if panel.current <> "" then m.optionsTab = panel.current
    m.optionsPanel = invalid
    m.optionsModel = ""
    m.optionsLayer.removeChild(panel)
    m.status.below = 0
    setOverlayFlags({ options: false, picker: false })
end sub

' The viewer's caption mode from Silo's UI, written to Roku's (plan section
' 6.10). It ends Replay's forced captions, so their end does not write
' "Instant replay" back over the choice.
sub setCaptionMode(mode as String)
    m.replayForced = false
    m.staleCaption = invalid
    if mode <> m.captionMode then m.staleCaption = { mode: m.captionMode, until: m.env.now() + STALE_CAPTION_MS }
    m.captionMode = mode
    noteWrite()
    m.video.globalCaptionMode = mode
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "caption mode chosen", { mode: mode })
end sub

' The viewer chose a track; a subtitle replaces one captions Off set aside,
' and the player selects its sidecar on its own again (confirmSubtitle).
sub trackChosen(subtitle as Boolean)
    if subtitle then m.burnWanted = invalid
    m.followedMode = invalid
    m.writeStops = { trackId: "", count: 0 }
end sub

' Roku's caption mode changed without a track choice, or a plan arrived
' (fromPlan): the plan may need a track_change to follow the mode
' (playback.options.captionTracks). Not while a track change is on its
' way: its plan comes back here. A plan's arrival asks once per mode, so a
' server that burns in a subtitle it was asked to leave out is not asked
' again until the mode or a track changes.
sub followCaptions(fromPlan as Boolean)
    if not fromPlan then m.followedMode = invalid
    if m.state = invalid or m.state.plan = invalid or playback.session.changingTracks(m.state) then return
    if fromPlan and m.followedMode <> invalid and m.followedMode = m.captionMode then return
    follow = playback.options.captionTracks(m.state.plan.data, m.captionMode, carriesSubtitles(), m.burnWanted)
    m.burnWanted = follow.wanted
    if follow.event = invalid then return
    if fromPlan then m.followedMode = m.captionMode
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "the plan follows the caption mode", { mode: m.captionMode, subtitle: follow.event.tracks.DoesExist("subtitle") })
    dispatch(follow.event)
end sub

' Whether the playing content of the current plan carries subtitle tracks.
function carriesSubtitles() as Boolean
    item = m.current
    if item = invalid or not item.assigned or m.activeLoad = invalid or m.activeLoad <> item.load then return false
    tracks = item.content.subtitleTracks
    return type(tracks) = "roArray" and tracks.Count() > 0
end function

' --- Seek previews --------------------------------------------------------------

' The previews follow the file the plan plays (plan section 6.9): a file
' the watch projection marks, on a server that lists trickplay_v1, has its
' manifest read; another shows the time alone. A replan that keeps the
' file keeps its manifest.
sub followPreviews(fileId as String)
    if fileId = m.previewFileId then return
    m.previewFileId = fileId
    if playback.trickplay.isEligible(m.watch, fileId, m.state.features)
        readPreviews()
        m.preview.manifest = playback.trickplay.pending()
    else
        playback.trickplay.cancel(m.previewFetch)
        m.previewFetch = invalid
        m.preview.manifest = {}
    end if
end sub

sub readPreviews()
    m.previewFetch = playback.trickplay.fetch(m.previewFetch, m.top.owner, m.itemId, m.previewFileId, serverBase(), "onPreviewManifest")
end sub

' The answer counts only on the latest read, for the file still playing
' (playback.trickplay.settle).
sub onPreviewManifest(event as Object)
    if m.closed then return
    manifest = playback.trickplay.settle(m.previewFetch, event.getRoSGNode(), m.previewFileId)
    if manifest <> invalid then m.preview.manifest = manifest
end sub

' The manifest's URLs expire, or a sheet failed: it is read again for the
' same file, and the preview keeps what it decoded meanwhile.
sub onPreviewRefresh()
    if m.closed or not m.preview.refresh or m.previewFetch = invalid then return
    readPreviews()
end sub

' The preview shows while the viewer scrubs, at its position: with the
' controls, a card centred over the scrub point and kept within the
' scrubber; with the ladder running from hidden controls, the tile at the
' top centre over the hold indicator (spec section 5.7).
sub updatePreview()
    c = m.controls
    scrubbing = playback.controls.isScrubbing(c)
    held = scrubbing and c.hiddenLadder
    active = scrubbing and (c.shown or held)
    if active
        m.preview.position = c.pending
        if held
            if m.preview.mode <> "hold" then m.preview.mode = "hold"
            m.preview.translation = [960, theme.player.HOLD_TOP]
            top = theme.player.HOLD_TOP
            if m.preview.heldHeight > 0 then top = top + m.preview.heldHeight + HOLD_GAP
            m.holdIndicator.translation = [960, top]
            m.holdIndicator.setFields({ rate: c.rate, position: c.pending, runtime: m.overlay.runtime })
        else
            if m.preview.mode <> "card" then m.preview.mode = "card"
            x = playback.trickplay.centerX(playback.trickplay.scrubPointX(c.pending, m.overlay.runtime, theme.player.LEFT, theme.player.RIGHT), m.preview.cardWidth, theme.player.LEFT, theme.player.RIGHT)
            m.preview.translation = [x, theme.player.PREVIEW_BOTTOM]
        end if
    end if
    if m.holdIndicator.visible <> held then m.holdIndicator.visible = held
    if m.preview.active <> active then m.preview.active = active
end sub

' --- Markers and Skip Intro ------------------------------------------------------

' The skip pills rise over the controls while they show, Options aside. A
' pill is lit while OK is its own: with the controls hidden (Skip Intro
' first), or while it has the controls' focus (spec section 5.7).
sub restyleSkipPills()
    c = m.controls
    shown = c.shown and not c.options
    idle = not c.shown and not c.options and not c.upNext
    m.skipButton.raised = shown
    m.skipButton.highlighted = idle or (shown and c.focus = playback.controls.SKIP_INTRO)
    m.recapButton.raised = shown
    m.recapButton.stacked = m.skipButton.visible
    m.recapButton.highlighted = (idle and not c.skipButton) or (shown and c.focus = playback.controls.SKIP_RECAP)
end sub

' The markers of the version a file belongs to, and the scrubber's bands.
sub readMarkers(fileId as String)
    m.markersFileId = fileId
    m.markers = []
    if util.isObject(m.version) then m.markers = playback.markers.fromVersion(m.version)
    m.overlay.markers = playback.markers.bands(m.markers)
end sub

' A plan's file: a replan that changes it reads its version's markers for
' the bands and Skip Intro, and Up Next takes the plan's runtime.
sub followMarkers(fileId as String)
    if fileId <> m.markersFileId
        readMarkers(fileId)
        runSkip({ type: "markers", markers: m.markers })
    end if
    runUpNext({ type: "timeline", runtime: m.state.plan.runtime })
end sub

' Reduces a Skip Intro event at the clock's now and carries out what it
' returns; Skip Recap takes the positions, the Video state, and the markers
' too.
sub runSkip(event as Object)
    if m.skip = invalid or m.leaving then return
    t = event.type
    if t = "position" or t = "player" or t = "markers" then runRecap(event)
    event.now = m.env.now()
    for each command in playback.skipIntro.reduce(m.skip, event)
        if command.type = "seek"
            commitSeek(command.seconds)
        else if command.type = "show"
            m.skipButton.mode = command.mode
            m.skipButton.progress = command.progress
            if not m.skipButton.visible
                m.skipButton.visible = true
                setOverlayFlags({ skipButton: true })
            end if
        else if command.type = "hide"
            hideSkip()
        end if
    end for
    schedulePanels()
end sub

sub hideSkip()
    if not m.skipButton.visible then return
    m.skipButton.visible = false
    setOverlayFlags({ skipButton: false })
end sub

' Reduces a Skip Recap event (playback.skipRecap): its seeks, a skip or the
' profile's auto-skip, go through the session reducer as every seek does.
sub runRecap(event as Object)
    if m.recap = invalid or m.leaving then return
    for each command in playback.skipRecap.reduce(m.recap, event)
        if command.type = "seek"
            commitSeek(command.seconds)
        else
            showRecap(command.type = "show")
        end if
    end for
end sub

sub showRecap(shown as Boolean)
    if m.recapButton.visible = shown then return
    m.recapButton.visible = shown
    setOverlayFlags({ recapButton: shown })
end sub

' OK with the skip button showing and the controls hidden.
sub activateSkip()
    runSkip({ type: "press" })
end sub

' Back with the skip button showing.
sub dismissSkip()
    runSkip({ type: "back" })
end sub

' A seek from the controls or Skip Intro, through the session reducer (a
' local seek or a seek_reanchor).
' resume: Play committed the seek while paused, so a load the seek opens
' plays (playback.session.onSeekTo).
sub commitSeek(position as Dynamic, resume = false as Boolean)
    dispatch({ type: "seekTo", position: position, resume: resume })
end sub

' Skip Intro's fill and Up Next's end countdown.
sub schedulePanels()
    now = m.env.now()
    wake = invalid
    if m.skip <> invalid then wake = playback.skipIntro.nextWake(m.skip, now)
    if m.upNext <> invalid then wake = sooner(wake, playback.upNext.nextWake(m.upNext, now))
    m.panelTimer.control = "stop"
    if wake = invalid or m.leaving then return
    delay = (wake - now) / 1000
    if delay < 0.01 then delay = 0.01
    m.panelTimer.duration = delay
    m.panelTimer.control = "start"
end sub

sub onPanelTimer()
    runSkip({ type: "tick" })
    runUpNext({ type: "tick" })
end sub

' --- Next episode, On Deck, and Up Next --------------------------------------------

' Up Next's reads once the first plan is in: the episode after this one
' (playback.nextEpisode), which settles at once with none for a movie or an
' episode the projection does not place in a series, and On Deck
' (playback.onDeck), both through ApiTask.
sub resolveNext()
    if m.upNext = invalid then return
    m.resolution = playback.nextEpisode.create(playback.nextEpisode.currentFromWatch(m.watch))
    sendNext(playback.nextEpisode.start(m.resolution))
    settleNext()
    m.onDeck = playback.onDeck.create({ itemId: m.itemId, seriesId: util.text(m.watch.series_id) }, isLowTier())
    sendOnDeck(playback.onDeck.start(m.onDeck))
    settleOnDeck()
end sub

sub sendNext(plans as Object)
    for each item in plans
        m.requests[api.send(item.request, handleFor("onNextEpisode"))] = { nextStage: item.stage }
    end for
end sub

' An answer for the resolution of the item still playing; one for an item
' before, or after the player closed, was dropped with its request.
sub onNextEpisode(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    context = takeRequest(handle)
    if context = invalid or m.resolution = invalid or m.closed then return
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    sendNext(playback.nextEpisode.answer(m.resolution, context.nextStage, result <> invalid and result.ok = true, handle.content))
    settleNext()
end sub

' Once settled, Up Next learns the next episode, as an entry, or that there
' is none.
sub settleNext()
    if not playback.nextEpisode.settled(m.resolution) then return
    found = playback.nextEpisode.episode(m.resolution)
    failed = playback.nextEpisode.failed(m.resolution)
    m.resolution = invalid
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "next episode", { found: found <> invalid, failed: failed })
    entry = invalid
    if found <> invalid then entry = { itemId: found.itemId, card: found.card, onDeck: false, seriesId: util.text(m.watch.series_id), seasonNumber: found.seasonNumber }
    runUpNext({ type: "next", next: entry, failed: failed })
end sub

sub sendOnDeck(plans as Object)
    for each item in plans
        m.requests[api.send(item.request, handleFor("onOnDeck"))] = { onDeckStage: item.stage }
    end for
end sub

sub onOnDeck(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    context = takeRequest(handle)
    if context = invalid or m.onDeck = invalid or m.closed then return
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    sendOnDeck(playback.onDeck.answer(m.onDeck, context.onDeckStage, result <> invalid and result.ok = true, handle.content))
    settleOnDeck()
end sub

sub settleOnDeck()
    if not playback.onDeck.settled(m.onDeck) then return
    items = playback.onDeck.entries(m.onDeck)
    m.onDeck = invalid
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "on deck", { items: items.Count() })
    runUpNext({ type: "onDeck", items: items })
end sub

' The controls' Up Next button shows while Up Next has something to show.
sub showUpNextButton(shown as Boolean)
    if m.overlay.episode = shown then return
    m.overlay.episode = shown
    dispatchControls({ type: "content", episode: shown })
end sub

' The Up Next button.
sub openUpNext()
    runUpNext({ type: "open" })
end sub

' Reduces an Up Next event at the clock's now and carries out what it
' returns.
sub runUpNext(event as Object)
    if m.upNext = invalid or m.leaving then return
    event.now = m.env.now()
    for each command in playback.upNext.reduce(m.upNext, event)
        t = command.type
        if t = "show"
            showUpNext(command)
        else if t = "close"
            closeUpNext()
        else if t = "resume"
            if m.video.state = "paused" then togglePause()
        else if t = "playNext"
            advanceTo(command)
        else if t = "replay"
            replayEnd(command.seconds)
        else if t = "exit"
            exitPlayer()
        end if
    end for
    if m.upNext <> invalid then showUpNextButton(playback.upNext.canOpen(m.upNext) or playback.upNext.isOpen(m.upNext))
    schedulePanels()
end sub

' The video ended. The session has stopped; Up Next holds the player, as
' Playing Next, or as Finished with nothing to play.
sub endOfVideo()
    m.videoEnded = true
    if m.upNext = invalid
        leavePlayer()
        return
    end if
    runUpNext({ type: "ended" })
end sub

' Opens the panel over the shrunken video, or gives it the command's
' heading, pick, countdown, toggle, and On Deck row. It closes Options and
' the controls and takes focus.
sub showUpNext(command as Object)
    panel = m.upNextPanel
    opening = panel = invalid
    if opening
        closeOptionsPanel()
        panel = m.upNextLayer.createChild("UpNextPanel")
        m.upNextPanel = panel
        panel.lowTier = isLowTier()
    end if
    panel.seriesTitle = pickSeries(command.pick)
    panel.setFields(playback.upNext.panelFields(command))
    if not opening then return
    panel.observeField("action", "onUpNextAction")
    panel.observeField("autoPlay", "onUpNextAutoPlay")
    panel.observeField("videoBox", "onUpNextBox")
    setVideoBox(panel.videoBox)
    panel.visible = true
    setOverlayFlags({ upNext: true })
    dispatchControls({ type: "hide" })
    panel.setFocus(true)
end sub

' The series line over the pick: the playing series' for its next episode,
' an On Deck episode's own, and none for a movie.
function pickSeries(entry as Dynamic) as String
    if entry = invalid then return ""
    if not entry.onDeck then return util.text(m.watch.series_title)
    card = entry.card
    if LCase(card.itemType) = "episode" then return card.caption
    return ""
end function

function isLowTier() as Boolean
    return util.text(platform.current().memory.tier) = "low"
end function

' The panel's text moved its video box.
sub onUpNextBox()
    if m.upNextPanel <> invalid then setVideoBox(m.upNextPanel.videoBox)
end sub

' The panel goes, and the video takes the screen and focus back.
sub closeUpNext()
    panel = m.upNextPanel
    if panel = invalid then return
    m.upNextPanel = invalid
    m.upNextLayer.removeChild(panel)
    setVideoBox(invalid)
    setOverlayFlags({ upNext: false })
end sub

' Play Now, Keep Watching, or Back on the panel, or OK on an On Deck card.
sub onUpNextAction()
    panel = m.upNextPanel
    if panel = invalid then return
    action = panel.action
    if action = "pick"
        runUpNext({ type: "pick", itemId: panel.picked })
    else
        runUpNext({ type: action })
    end if
end sub

' The panel's toggle is Options' Auto-play next too.
sub onUpNextAutoPlay()
    panel = m.upNextPanel
    if panel = invalid or m.upNext = invalid or panel.autoPlay = m.upNext.autoPlay then return
    chooseAutoplay(panel.autoPlay)
end sub

' The viewer turned Auto-play next on or off, in Options or on the panel:
' tvOS keeps the choice in the profile's playback.auto_play_next for this
' device.
sub chooseAutoplay(value as Boolean)
    m.autoplayChosen = true
    setAutoplay(value)
    writeAutoplay(value)
end sub

' Auto-play next, for Options and Up Next alike.
sub setAutoplay(value as Boolean)
    m.autoplayNext = value
    runUpNext({ type: "autoPlay", value: value })
    refreshOptions()
end sub

' Writes the toggle for this device, as Settings does; a failed write
' leaves the profile as it was, and the toggle holds for this player.
sub writeAutoplay(value as Boolean)
    m.preferences.autoPlayNext = value
    request = playback.preferences.autoPlayWrite(value)
    m.requests[api.send(request, handleFor("onAutoplayWritten"))] = "autoplayWrite"
end sub

sub onAutoplayWritten(event as Object)
    handle = event.getRoSGNode()
    takeRequest(handle)
    result = api.resultOf(handle)
    if result = invalid or result.ok <> true
        status = 0
        if result <> invalid then status = result.status
        log.warn(LOG_TAG, "auto-play next could not be saved", { status: status })
    end if
end sub

' Play Now, the countdown, or an On Deck card: the session stops with its
' final position, as Back stops it (plan section 6.6), then the next item
' starts here.
sub advanceTo(command as Object)
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "playing the next item", { auto: command.auto, chosen: command.chosen, onDeck: command.onDeck })
    closeUpNext()
    season = -1
    pick = m.upNext.next
    if pick <> invalid and pick.itemId = command.itemId and util.isNumber(pick.seasonNumber) then season = Int(pick.seasonNumber)
    m.advance = { itemId: command.itemId, carry: command.carry, seasonNumber: season, auto: not command.chosen, replay: invalid, foreign: command.onDeck }
    if not m.done then dispatch({ type: "back" })
    advanceWhenDone()
end sub

' Keep Watching after the end: the same item again from seconds.
sub replayEnd(seconds as Dynamic)
    log.info(LOG_TAG, "replaying the end", { seconds: seconds })
    closeUpNext()
    m.advance = { itemId: m.itemId, carry: playback.upNext.replayCarry(m.upNext), seasonNumber: playingSeason(), auto: false, replay: seconds, foreign: false }
    if not m.done then dispatch({ type: "back" })
    advanceWhenDone()
end sub

' Once the session the advance ends is done, and no reduction is under way.
' An item of another title tells the entry's page about the last one of the
' first title first, as the player leaving would.
sub advanceWhenDone()
    if m.advance = invalid or not m.done or m.dispatching or m.leaving or m.closed then return
    chosen = m.advance
    m.advance = invalid
    if chosen.foreign and not m.leftSeries
        notePlayedLast()
        m.leftSeries = true
    end if
    clearSession()
    m.itemId = chosen.itemId
    m.itemSeason = chosen.seasonNumber
    m.startOver = false
    if chosen.replay <> invalid
        m.wanted = nav.player.replay(chosen.itemId, chosen.replay, chosen.carry)
    else
        m.wanted = nav.player.nextEpisode(chosen.itemId, chosen.carry, chosen.auto)
    end if
    loadWatch()
end sub

' What belonged to the item that ended goes before the next one starts
' in this player. Its session is done; the Video node stops, and the next
' content waits for that (playback.slot). The profile's preferences stay.
sub clearSession()
    closeOptionsPanel()
    closeUpNext()
    hideSkip()
    showRecap(false)
    m.progressTimer.control = "stop"
    m.panelTimer.control = "stop"
    replayCaptions(false)
    cancelSubtitle()
    stopMediaTask()
    m.mediaQueue = []
    runSlot(playback.slot.halt(m.slot, m.video.state, m.env.now()))
    playback.trickplay.cancel(m.previewFetch)
    m.previewFetch = invalid
    m.previewFileId = ""
    m.preview.active = false
    dropRequests()
    m.loads = m.state.loads
    m.state = invalid
    m.intent = invalid
    m.watch = invalid
    m.version = invalid
    m.picks = invalid
    m.firstPlan = true
    m.current = invalid
    m.activeLoad = invalid
    m.activeProxy = false
    m.activePlayed = false
    m.activeTrack = ""
    m.activeStarted = false
    m.subtitleConfirmed = false
    m.recheckAt = invalid
    m.wroteAt = invalid
    m.writeStops = { trackId: "", count: 0 }
    m.pauseLoad = invalid
    m.flags = newFlags()
    m.noticeClock = playback.player.newNoticeClock(0)
    m.overlayWatch = { played: false, audio: "", subtitle: "" }
    m.burnWanted = invalid
    m.followedMode = invalid
    m.markers = []
    m.markersFileId = ""
    m.skip = invalid
    m.recap = invalid
    m.upNext = invalid
    m.resolution = invalid
    m.onDeck = invalid
    m.videoEnded = false
    m.done = false
    dispatchControls({ type: "hide" })
    ' Replay's caption span was the episode's; replayCaptions ended it.
    m.controls.replay = invalid
end sub

' Drops the answers the episode before still waits for, but the profile's
' preferences and an output probe, which hold for the next one too.
sub dropRequests()
    kept = {}
    for each id in m.requests
        context = m.requests[id]
        if util.isString(context) and (context = "preferences" or context = "outputContext") then kept[id] = context
    end for
    m.requests = kept
end sub

' The overlays above report themselves: flags has any of skipButton,
' picker, upNext, and options.
sub setOverlayFlags(flags as Object)
    event = { type: "flags" }
    event.Append(flags)
    dispatchControls(event)
    ' Raised while a command runs (a key opening Options, whose list then
    ' takes focus), the event waits behind it, and focus waits for the
    ' event: deciding it now, from flags not yet reduced, took focus from
    ' the panel's list (run 6).
    if m.controlsBusy
        m.refocus = true
    else
        applyFocus()
    end if
end sub

' Up Next's 16:9 frame on the left, { x, y, width, height } in FHD px, or
' invalid for the full screen.
sub setVideoBox(frame as Dynamic)
    if frame = invalid then frame = { x: 0, y: 0, width: 1920, height: 1080 }
    m.video.translation = [frame.x, frame.y]
    m.video.width = frame.width
    m.video.height = frame.height
end sub

' A notice shows for NOTICE_MS once nothing outranks it on the status
' line, whatever showed when it came (playback.player.noticeShows).
sub notice(text as String)
    m.flags.notice = text
    m.noticeClock = playback.player.newNoticeClock(NOTICE_MS)
end sub

' The overlay's position, runtime, and play state, the status, the
' controls reducer's view of playback, and the Options panel.
sub refreshChrome()
    if m.closed then return
    now = m.env.now()
    position = 0#
    runtime = invalid
    seeking = false
    if m.state <> invalid
        position = m.state.player.position
        ' A seek in flight shows, and counts skips from, its target.
        if util.isNumber(m.state.seekTarget) then position = m.state.seekTarget
        seeking = util.isNumber(m.state.seekTarget) or m.state.player.seeking
        if m.state.plan <> invalid then runtime = m.state.plan.runtime
    end if
    if runtime = invalid and m.intent <> invalid then runtime = m.intent.runtime
    buffering = m.video.state = "buffering"
    paused = m.video.state = "paused"
    flags = { buffering: buffering }
    flags.Append(m.flags)
    if flags.notice <> "" and not playback.player.noticeShows(m.noticeClock, flags, now)
        m.flags.notice = ""
        flags.notice = ""
    end if
    ' Under the error the status is out of sight, and says nothing.
    status = { busy: "", notice: invalid }
    if not m.errorVisible then status = playback.player.statusOf(flags)
    m.status.busy = status.busy
    if status.notice = invalid then m.status.notice = {} else m.status.notice = status.notice
    m.overlay.paused = paused
    m.overlay.position = position
    if runtime = invalid then m.overlay.runtime = 0 else m.overlay.runtime = runtime
    busy = seeking or buffering or m.flags.starting or m.flags.reconnecting
    dispatchControls({ type: "playback", position: position, runtime: runtime, paused: paused, busy: busy })
    refreshOptions()
end sub

' --- Requests ---------------------------------------------------------------------

function handleFor(callback as String) as Object
    handle = api.newHandle(m.top.owner)
    handle.observeField("status", callback)
    return handle
end function

' What the answered request was for, or invalid when it was dropped.
function takeRequest(handle as Object) as Dynamic
    id = handle.requestId
    context = m.requests[id]
    m.requests.Delete(id)
    return context
end function
